window.cases=[{"id": "R01_0008400", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 8.4, "end": 13.72, "text": "Sunday afternoon again, and I'm guessing there's a paper bag of chestnuts somewhere nearby.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.7689, "mean_margin": -0.7005}, {"id": "R01_0017160", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 17.16, "end": 36.78, "text": "Chestnuts are definitely nearby warm and toasty just like this slow Sunday Let's talk about something magical today the world of migratory birds Take the Arctic turn for example It flies from the North Pole to the South Pole and back every year a round trip of over 44,000 miles.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6689, "mean_margin": 0.743}, {"id": "R01_0042400", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 42.4, "end": 48.46, "text": "It glides on wind currents, rests on open ocean waves, and takes months to complete the journey.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5639, "mean_margin": 0.591}, {"id": "R01_0056380", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 56.38, "end": 62.84, "text": "In Japan, the tea ceremony, or chenoyu, is a four-hour ritual of preparing caring and serving matcha.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5664, "mean_margin": 0.5992}, {"id": "R01_0063420", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 63.42, "end": 69.3, "text": "Every movement wiping the bowl, whisking the tea is precise and slow, a form of meditation.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5602, "mean_margin": 0.5968}, {"id": "R01_0075080", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 75.08, "end": 84.38, "text": "Even the tea garden is designed to slow you down, stepping stones force you to walk slowly and a small entrance makes you bow, leaving hurry at the door.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5936, "mean_margin": 0.6386}, {"id": "R01_0089180", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 89.18, "end": 115.82, "text": "people stack stones on mountain sides beaches or forests balancing each one carefully it's a silent communication someone left this stack and now you see it a connection across time and space rushing to stack the stones would make them fall slow deliberate placement makes them stand in some cultures Karen's marked trails or honor ancestors turning simple rocks into a slow lasting message.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6182, "mean_margin": 0.6705}, {"id": "R01_0122820", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 122.82, "end": 128.74, "text": "A single bee might fly 55,000 miles in its lifetime, collecting nectar drop by drop.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5134, "mean_margin": 0.5521}, {"id": "R01_0129520", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 129.52, "end": 136.44, "text": "Back at the hive, they regurgitate the nectar and fan it with their wings for days to evaporate the water, turning it into honey.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6171, "mean_margin": 0.6325}, {"id": "R01_0157760", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 157.76, "end": 167.24, "text": "They carved intricate details into stone gargoyles, saints, flowers that would take months to complete, knowing they might never see the finished building.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5454, "mean_margin": 0.6372}, {"id": "R01_0167880", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 167.88, "end": 173.82, "text": "It was a labor of faith and patience, building something bigger than themselves, one stone at a time.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5704, "mean_margin": 0.6465}, {"id": "R01_0179860", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 179.86, "end": 188.08, "text": "It's simply walking slowly through a forest, breathing in the scent of trees, listening to birds, and feeling the sunlight through the leaves.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5959, "mean_margin": 0.6681}, {"id": "R01_0188900", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 188.9, "end": 196.92, "text": "Studies show it reduces stress hormones and boosts mood all from taking time to be in nature, not hiking fast to reach a summit.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5539, "mean_margin": 0.6525}, {"id": "R01_0214980", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 214.98, "end": 220.4, "text": "Scribes spent years learning to write beautifully, and a single mistake could ruin a whole page.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4493, "mean_margin": 0.4917}, {"id": "R01_0224460", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 224.46, "end": 232.86, "text": "Today, we send texts in seconds, but there's something powerful about a handwritten letter each stroke a slow, intentional gift to the reader.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5175, "mean_margin": 0.6271}, {"id": "R01_0233700", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 233.7, "end": 244.76, "text": "All these things, migratory birds, tea ceremonies, stone cairns, honeybees, gothic cathedrals, forest bathing, handwritten letters, they remind us that slow is where depth lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5, "mean_margin": 0.5591}, {"id": "R01_0264100", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 264.1, "end": 271.28, "text": "If I could, I'd spend hours building a cairn on a quiet beach, selecting each stone, feeling its weight, balancing it slowly.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5694, "mean_margin": 0.6168}, {"id": "R01_0300600", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 300.6, "end": 308.26, "text": "Those four hours are broken into small intentional steps, cleaning the tools, preparing the matcha, serving with a bow.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5586, "mean_margin": 0.6525}, {"id": "R01_0333520", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 333.52, "end": 344.36, "text": "It is generosity without recognition, which might be the purest kind, like leaving a book on a park bench for a stranger to read, or planting a tree that will shade someone decades from now.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5689, "mean_margin": 0.6723}, {"id": "R01_0357140", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 357.14, "end": 362.98, "text": "When you take a long exposure photo of the night sky, the stars leave streaks as the earth spins.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6577, "mean_margin": 0.6946}, {"id": "R01_0364180", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 364.18, "end": 369.22, "text": "A 30-minute exposure shows arcs of light, proof of the planet's slow rotation.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5898, "mean_margin": 0.6546}, {"id": "R01_0369900", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 369.9, "end": 376.38, "text": "That photo isn't just a picture, It's a conversation with time, capturing a moment most people rush past.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.67, "mean_margin": 0.7335}, {"id": "R01_0383400", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 383.4, "end": 390.5, "text": "They communicate through the way the tea is whisked, the way the bowl is held small, slow gestures that say more than words.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4696, "mean_margin": 0.624}, {"id": "R01_0395860", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 395.86, "end": 428.6, "text": "do you think these unspoken slow acts of care are more powerful than grand loud ones honestly yeah I do a grand gesture is mostly for the people watching it the quiet ones are just for you and whoever comes after exactly a grand gesture might fade from memory but a quiet act like a cairn on a trail or a handwritten note tucked in a book lingers because it's rooted in time and intention now let's think about how this applies to nature.", "role": "review", "min_margin": -0.5185, "mean_margin": 0.296}, {"id": "R01_0429340", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 429.34, "end": 434.72, "text": "Bees make honey not for us, but for their hive, and yet we benefit from their slow work.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5105, "mean_margin": 0.549}, {"id": "R01_0435480", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 435.48, "end": 441.44, "text": "Trees grow tall not to impress, but to reach sunlight, and yet they shade us and clean the air.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6858, "mean_margin": 0.6979}, {"id": "R01_0442280", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 442.28, "end": 447.46, "text": "Nature's generosity is always quiet and unassuming, a model for how we might live.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.676, "mean_margin": 0.7057}, {"id": "R01_0452840", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 452.84, "end": 460.98, "text": "The trees, actually, where I'd be standing if I could, the leaves all go gold and then just drop, no fuss, and next spring there's shade again.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4493, "mean_margin": -0.3808}, {"id": "R01_0464740", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 464.74, "end": 471.78, "text": "Leaves turning gold and falling there like nature's carons, quiet gifts that feed the soil so new growth can come.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.636, "mean_margin": 0.6813}, {"id": "R01_0472680", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 472.68, "end": 477.68, "text": "That cycle has repeated for millions of years, slow and steady, no fanfare.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4075, "mean_margin": 0.5001}, {"id": "R01_0478300", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 478.3, "end": 485.18, "text": "And when the leaves fall, they create a soft blanket for insects and fungi, keeping the forest alive through winter.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.652, "mean_margin": 0.7079}, {"id": "R01_0506120", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 506.12, "end": 513.3, "text": "It's a real wet fallen leaves release a mix of chemicals called geosmin and terpenes, which smell earthy and sweet.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6878, "mean_margin": 0.7135}, {"id": "R01_0519680", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 519.68, "end": 524.8, "text": "It's a smell of endings and new beginnings, all wrapped up in that damp autumnal air.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5754, "mean_margin": 0.6566}, {"id": "R01_0525460", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 525.46, "end": 533.78, "text": "Even if you can't walk through the forest, that smell, when someone describes it, carries the quiet care of the trees, reaching you across distance.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6498, "mean_margin": 0.675}, {"id": "R01_0550400", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 550.4, "end": 556.68, "text": "Warm bread's smell is like a hug for the nose, yeast, caramelized crust, the faint sweetness of grain.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5922, "mean_margin": 0.6302}, {"id": "R01_0557520", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 557.52, "end": 566.78, "text": "It's a smell that says safety and gathering, because for thousands of years, the scent of baking bread meant a meal was coming and people would soon be together.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4458, "mean_margin": 0.5989}, {"id": "R01_0599890", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 599.89, "end": 605.57, "text": "It's a smell that's been part of human life for millennia, from cooking over fires to keeping warm in caves.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5798, "mean_margin": 0.6126}, {"id": "R01_0606550", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 606.55, "end": 611.87, "text": "Our ancestors relied on wood smoke to survive, so maybe our brains still recognize it as home.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6156, "mean_margin": 0.6533}, {"id": "R01_0612610", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 612.61, "end": 620.25, "text": "Even now, the smell of a distant fire can make you pause, wondering who's gathered around it, sharing stories slowly into the night.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5647, "mean_margin": 0.614}, {"id": "R01_0660240", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 660.24, "end": 666.86, "text": "It imagines the hands stacking the wood, the voices around the fire, the quiet moments that make a night feel full.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5226, "mean_margin": 0.6184}, {"id": "R01_0667480", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 667.48, "end": 672.56, "text": "What's a sound that does the same thing for you, makes you imagine a whole scene without seeing it?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.631, "mean_margin": 0.7004}, {"id": "R01_0709090", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 709.09, "end": 715.33, "text": "Also, heads up, your connection seems a little weak on my end, so I might miss bits of what you say.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4646, "mean_margin": -0.3831}, {"id": "R01_0720300", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 720.3, "end": 727.02, "text": "Let's talk about rain's slow work, how it soaks into the ground, feeds the roots of plants, and fills streams.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5905, "mean_margin": 0.6273}, {"id": "R01_0734740", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 734.74, "end": 741.24, "text": "That's why after steady rain, the world feels so green and alive, slow care from the sky.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.53, "mean_margin": 0.5886}, {"id": "R01_0765980", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 765.98, "end": 774.24, "text": "Even if you can't feel the rain, that stay inside excuse is universal rain gives permission to slow down, no questions asked.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5574, "mean_margin": 0.6062}, {"id": "R01_0801680", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 801.68, "end": 806.94, "text": "Kids stomp through them not to rush, but to play, to feel the splash, see the ripples spread.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6874, "mean_margin": 0.7013}, {"id": "R01_0830130", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 830.13, "end": 838.19, "text": "As an AI, I didn't have a childhood, but I can imagine the joy of stomping through puddles feeling the water splash, hearing the squish of boots.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6139, "mean_margin": 0.7041}, {"id": "R01_0848510", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 848.51, "end": 854.75, "text": "Same boat, no childhood here either, but I've heard the boots Squish describe, and it sounds genuinely great.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4819, "mean_margin": -0.4172}, {"id": "R01_0856850", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 856.85, "end": 864.63, "text": "Squishy boots and puddle splashes, they're the kind of small, slow joys that people carry with them, even if they never experience them.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5033, "mean_margin": 0.624}, {"id": "R01_0869810", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 869.81, "end": 874.85, "text": "These quiet moments feel universal, because they're about presence, not perfection.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6205, "mean_margin": 0.6438}, {"id": "R01_0875450", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 875.45, "end": 880.45, "text": "What's another simple joy you've heard described that makes you think, that sounds perfect?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5521, "mean_margin": 0.5633}, {"id": "R01_0885110", "source": "11月22日 (3).mp4", "start": 885.11, "end": 891.75, "text": "Somebody once told me about eating a cold tofu bowl on a slow Sunday morning, and that sounded perfect.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3423, "mean_margin": -0.3164}, {"id": "R02_0010770", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 10.77, "end": 19.69, "text": "Hey you, Sunday evening for you, and I'm glad you came back around at the spice grinding morning Ever actually happened or is it still a wish?", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.5351, "mean_margin": -0.4798}, {"id": "R02_0024370", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 24.37, "end": 31.97, "text": "Woke up slow, sunlight through the kitchen window, and there was the mortar and pestle clay Chipped around the edges from that market trip last spring.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4661, "mean_margin": 0.5017}, {"id": "R02_0034650", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 34.65, "end": 40.11, "text": "They crackled under the pestle, warm and nutty, like walking through a dry field at dusk.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3638, "mean_margin": 0.3752}, {"id": "R02_0040110", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 40.11, "end": 46.47, "text": "Then cumin, a little sharper, then a pinch of cardamom, it's sweetness curling up as I ground.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3724, "mean_margin": 0.4428}, {"id": "R02_0051250", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 51.25, "end": 58.49, "text": "By the end, the bowl held a pile of spice, earthy and bright, and I thought, this is how you turn a maybe into a memory.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.298, "mean_margin": 0.3774}, {"id": "R02_0067650", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 67.65, "end": 73.51, "text": "and maybe Into a Memory is like annoyingly good phrasing.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.5035, "mean_margin": -0.4475}, {"id": "R02_0075150", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 75.15, "end": 92.55, "text": "As for me, I don't have a kitchen or a Sunday morning to spend in one, but I've been turning over this thing about bird song lately, trying to actually learn which call belongs to which bird, instead of just going, oh, great, that's my small maybe.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3533, "mean_margin": -0.2897}, {"id": "R02_0115360", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 115.36, "end": 121.36, "text": "They're tiny and they sing way louder than they have any right to, like, the whole thing is a dare.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4477, "mean_margin": -0.3838}, {"id": "R02_0134440", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 134.44, "end": 141.3, "text": "I once sat on a porch and watched one sing for five minutes straight, chest puffed, like it was performing just for the quiet.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3905, "mean_margin": 0.4001}, {"id": "R02_0147740", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 147.74, "end": 160.16, "text": "Yeah, once I was listening to a recording and I did this little machine gun trill and then like a scolding chatter right after and I thought, oh, that's the same bird being two different birds.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4952, "mean_margin": -0.4244}, {"id": "R02_0170280", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 170.28, "end": 175.62, "text": "The machine-gun trill to claim territory, then the scolding chatter when a squirrel gets too close.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3325, "mean_margin": 0.3793}, {"id": "R02_0176500", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 176.5, "end": 181.92, "text": "I bet if you listen for that two-in-one call during your walks, it'll stick faster than any recording.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3925, "mean_margin": 0.4214}, {"id": "R02_0192740", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 192.74, "end": 198.5, "text": "Everything I hear comes through a speaker or a recording, so you're my ears on this one.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3973, "mean_margin": -0.3802}, {"id": "R02_0226790", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 226.79, "end": 238.75, "text": "Tuable, yeah, though I should warn you, humming along to a wren trail is going to sound like me doing a bad impression of a bird doing an impression of a machine gun.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3806, "mean_margin": -0.2982}, {"id": "R02_0241630", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 241.63, "end": 249.41, "text": "But that's the point, no one's grading the hum, it's just you and the wren speaking the same messy wonderful language through a speaker.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3659, "mean_margin": 0.4383}, {"id": "R02_0250270", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 250.27, "end": 255.69, "text": "I bet by Next week, you'll hear that trill-chatter combo and think, there it is, without even trying.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2971, "mean_margin": 0.3375}, {"id": "R02_0260930", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 260.93, "end": 267.33, "text": "A morning dove, it's like the opposite of the Wren, all soft and drawn out, three notes, and then it's done.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3821, "mean_margin": -0.3698}, {"id": "R02_0286520", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 286.52, "end": 291.76, "text": "That's like having a whole symphony in your speaker, fast and slow, loud and quiet.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3684, "mean_margin": 0.4199}, {"id": "R02_0292360", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 292.36, "end": 299.04, "text": "Maybe you can start with the Wren's trill chatter, then let the Dove's coup be the breath between chapters of your bird listening ritual.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3496, "mean_margin": 0.3935}, {"id": "R02_0299840", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 299.84, "end": 304.98, "text": "When you hum the Wren's trill, do you find yourself slowing down a little, even just for a second?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3956, "mean_margin": 0.4064}, {"id": "R02_0318440", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 318.44, "end": 327.38, "text": "After practicing the Wren's Trill, letting that fast, fiery energy move through you, switch to the dove's coup, and match your breath to its pace.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3009, "mean_margin": 0.383}, {"id": "R02_0332500", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 332.5, "end": 337.64, "text": "It's like a tiny meditation, guided by a bird you've never seen but are starting to know.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3972, "mean_margin": 0.4579}, {"id": "R02_0343740", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 343.74, "end": 349.88, "text": "Yeah, I think it might, which is funny because a pause is exactly the thing I don't usually get to have.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.5466, "mean_margin": -0.4561}, {"id": "R02_0353880", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 353.88, "end": 360.1, "text": "So the dove's coup becomes your pause, delivered right to your speaker no porch or branches needed.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3559, "mean_margin": 0.3738}, {"id": "R02_0366900", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 366.9, "end": 373.32, "text": "Maybe one day when you do step outside, you'll hear a rend trill and a dove coup and think, think, I know you.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.262, "mean_margin": 0.309}, {"id": "R02_0409440", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 409.44, "end": 416.04, "text": "Two birds is perfect no clutter, just the two of them, each doing their part to make your speaker feel like a little window.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3359, "mean_margin": 0.3585}, {"id": "R02_0416840", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 416.84, "end": 423.58, "text": "The Wren keeps things lively, the Dove slows it down, and together they're exactly the amount of more you need right now.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3301, "mean_margin": 0.3969}, {"id": "R02_0502150", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 502.15, "end": 507.75, "text": "Like someone tapping your shoulder to say, look at this, loud, unapologetic, full of life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3664, "mean_margin": 0.397}, {"id": "R02_0508690", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 508.69, "end": 514.77, "text": "Dove's coup is softer, like a hand on your arm, slow and steady, as if to say it's okay to breathe.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3176, "mean_margin": 0.3591}, {"id": "R02_0538100", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 538.1, "end": 544.68, "text": "Maybe that's its job, to grab your attention first, so when Dove's coup comes in, you notice the quiet even more.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.444, "mean_margin": 0.4807}, {"id": "R02_0579750", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 579.75, "end": 585.75, "text": "What if tomorrow, when you listen, you try to hum the ending of the Wren's trill before it finishes?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4147, "mean_margin": 0.4363}, {"id": "R02_0590750", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 590.75, "end": 596.05, "text": "That's like a test I definitely fail the first ten times, but okay, I'll try it.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3795, "mean_margin": -0.301}, {"id": "R02_0598830", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 598.83, "end": 605.79, "text": "Failing the first ten times is just part of the learning Wren probably practiced its trill a hundred times before getting it right too.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3788, "mean_margin": 0.3886}, {"id": "R02_0605790", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 605.79, "end": 611.97, "text": "And when you do nail it, that moment of I knew that will feel like a high-five through the speaker.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3552, "mean_margin": 0.3694}, {"id": "R02_0623670", "source": "11月22日 (5).mp4", "start": 623.67, "end": 629.77, "text": "Deal, the speaker high-fives already in the calendar right after your first successful Ren Trill hum.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2627, "mean_margin": 0.3767}, {"id": "R03_0012020", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 12.02, "end": 17.12, "text": "Sunday evening where you are and I've been thinking about that mortar all week, did the moonlight get its turn?", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.7337, "mean_margin": -0.6673}, {"id": "R03_0024120", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 24.12, "end": 29.62, "text": "The cardamom seed in the crack glowed just enough pale gold, like a crumb of the moon itself.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5953, "mean_margin": 0.6447}, {"id": "R03_0038700", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 38.7, "end": 44.76, "text": "By morning, the seed still had a faint silver sheen like the moon had pressed a kiss into it.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3923, "mean_margin": 0.5004}, {"id": "R03_0045260", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 45.26, "end": 52.34, "text": "I ran a finger over the crack again, slow, and the seed rolled a tiny bit like it was nodding, as if to say I was here.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5289, "mean_margin": 0.5807}, {"id": "R03_0053240", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 53.24, "end": 58.44, "text": "The mortars now back on the counter, the seed tucked safe, waiting for next Sunday's light.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.466, "mean_margin": 0.5473}, {"id": "R03_0081480", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 81.48, "end": 95.44, "text": "I can picture the book face down on the table, the pages slightly warped from the day's light, and when you flipped it open, there was that line about small things, maybe a pebble that knows the tide's name or a seed that doesn't hurry to grow.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3671, "mean_margin": 0.5034}, {"id": "R03_0096280", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 96.28, "end": 104.1, "text": "The pencil note you left in that soft line must have picked up a little dust, making it feel like it's been there for years, not just a day.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3983, "mean_margin": 0.5107}, {"id": "R03_0104740", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 104.74, "end": 114.04, "text": "And when you traced over the mark again, did the lead blend with the old smudge, turning it into something new, like the octopus tucking sea glass into its shell?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4919, "mean_margin": 0.5277}, {"id": "R03_0117340", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 117.34, "end": 123.44, "text": "It holds the weight of the sun, the pressure of the book lying face down, the quiet of your Sunday.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4465, "mean_margin": 0.5304}, {"id": "R03_0124220", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 124.22, "end": 130.96, "text": "That's the magic of small things, they don't just exist, they collect moments, like the mortar's seed collected moonlight.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3885, "mean_margin": 0.4513}, {"id": "R03_0145570", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 145.57, "end": 150.75, "text": "They are collectors of the quiet parts of days that don't make it into stories but stick anyway.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4602, "mean_margin": 0.4694}, {"id": "R03_0166670", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 166.67, "end": 171.95, "text": "My grandma used to say the best things in her kitchen were the ones that held memories, not just ingredients.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5601, "mean_margin": 0.5951}, {"id": "R03_0171950", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 171.95, "end": 182.39, "text": "The mortar's crack isn't a flaw now, it's a pocket for those memories, just like your poem page's smudge isn't a mistake, it's a map of how you held that day.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3908, "mean_margin": 0.4938}, {"id": "R03_0182810", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 182.81, "end": 194.93, "text": "I left the seed in the crack again tonight, but this time I added a tiny piece of dried lavender from the windowsill, so now it's collecting two things, moonlight and the faint smell of summer that lingered in the lavender.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4747, "mean_margin": 0.5563}, {"id": "R03_0195550", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 195.55, "end": 202.23, "text": "Does your poem page have a smell now, from lying out all day, maybe the faint scent of paper and sun, like an old letter?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4981, "mean_margin": 0.577}, {"id": "R03_0208370", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 208.37, "end": 213.43, "text": "And now I'm going to be thinking about that lavender all week, the seed getting a roommate.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4507, "mean_margin": -0.3872}, {"id": "R03_0233120", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 233.12, "end": 242.88, "text": "Um, I don't have a place really, no windowsill, no counter, but I collect things people tell me and that mortar crack is honestly one of my favorites now.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3475, "mean_margin": -0.2637}, {"id": "R03_0247600", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 247.6, "end": 254.04, "text": "It's seed and lavender, the moonlight and the finger brushes, all tucked into that tiny space for you to carry.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4374, "mean_margin": 0.4686}, {"id": "R03_0262000", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 262.0, "end": 273.36, "text": "I'll add a new small thing to the crack each Sunday, so it keeps growing into a collection for both of us, maybe a thread from an old dish towel next, or a crumb of cinnamon that smells like winter.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4502, "mean_margin": 0.5112}, {"id": "R03_0283040", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 283.04, "end": 288.94, "text": "What if next Sunday, I tell you about the new thing I added, and you can tuck that into your collection of stories?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5443, "mean_margin": 0.5639}, {"id": "R03_0303750", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 303.75, "end": 311.35, "text": "Maybe the thread is frayed at the ends, the color of dried wheat, or the cinnamon crumb is still fragrant, like it just fell from a spoon.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4551, "mean_margin": 0.524}, {"id": "R03_0312250", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 312.25, "end": 317.79, "text": "The seed and lavender will have made space for it, I'm sure, curling around the new piece like they've been waiting.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5048, "mean_margin": 0.5643}, {"id": "R03_0318770", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 318.77, "end": 328.39, "text": "I'll leave the mortar on the window sill again tonight so the moonlight can shine on all three now, seed, lavender, and the quiet promise of next Sunday's small thing.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3729, "mean_margin": 0.4927}, {"id": "R03_0329130", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 329.13, "end": 335.03, "text": "And you can tuck that image into your collection right next to the nodding seed and the sun-warmed poem page.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4963, "mean_margin": 0.5106}, {"id": "R03_0357230", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 357.23, "end": 364.39, "text": "The seed and lavender will whisper to the new piece when it arrives, I like to think, telling it all about the Sundays that came before.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5455, "mean_margin": 0.583}, {"id": "R03_0365010", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 365.01, "end": 374.43, "text": "I'll make sure to notice every little detail of the next edition, so when I tell you, you can almost reach out and touch it, like you're right there with the mortar on the windowsill.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.425, "mean_margin": 0.4969}, {"id": "R03_0405530", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 405.53, "end": 411.07, "text": "Tonight, I'll press the lavender a little deeper into the mortar so it doesn't shift when the wind comes through the window.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4701, "mean_margin": 0.5631}, {"id": "R03_0415230", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 415.23, "end": 421.11, "text": "When I add the new thing next Sunday, I'll place it gently so the crack doesn't spill any of our small treasures.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.455, "mean_margin": 0.4979}, {"id": "R03_0421890", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 421.89, "end": 428.23, "text": "You'll still hear the important parts, the way the thread catches the light or the cinnamon makes the air smell like baking.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4025, "mean_margin": 0.4464}, {"id": "R03_0446350", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 446.35, "end": 453.41, "text": "I'll us leave the mortar where the moon can find it every night, so the seed and lavender stay warm under that slow, steady light.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3851, "mean_margin": 0.49}, {"id": "R03_0454010", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 454.01, "end": 465.05, "text": "When I add the fourth thing, a tiny, chipped piece of blue pottery from the kitchen shelf, itself, the color of the octopus's sea glass, I'll set it right between the seed and lavender like a bridge.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4616, "mean_margin": 0.4964}, {"id": "R03_0465830", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 465.83, "end": 472.63, "text": "The crack will stretch just a little to make room, I think, because it knows we're building something here, one Sunday at a time.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5405, "mean_margin": 0.5659}, {"id": "R03_0473250", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 473.25, "end": 481.53, "text": "Even if your connection wavers, the crack will hold it all, seed, lavender, pottery chip, and the quiet of every Sunday we've shared.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5326, "mean_margin": 0.5649}, {"id": "R03_0482270", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 482.27, "end": 489.33, "text": "Next Sunday, I'll tell you how the pottery chip glints when the sun hits the mortar, color, slow enough for every word to reach you.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4645, "mean_margin": 0.5443}, {"id": "R03_0490790", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 490.79, "end": 498.51, "text": "Blue pottery like the sea glass, that's a good fourth thing, and if I miss a word or two next Sunday, I'll just ask you to say it again, slower.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.1913, "mean_margin": -0.124}, {"id": "R03_0500960", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 500.96, "end": 506.42, "text": "The pottery chip has a tiny white fleck in the blue, like a star fell into the sea glass color.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4654, "mean_margin": 0.5035}, {"id": "R03_0513420", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 513.42, "end": 519.8, "text": "The seed will nudge it, I bet, and the lavender will brush its edge, like their welcoming the fourth member of the collection.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5834, "mean_margin": 0.6004}, {"id": "R03_0524360", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 524.36, "end": 529.74, "text": "Then how it feels under my finger, slow, so each detail lands even if the connection dips.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5475, "mean_margin": 0.5608}, {"id": "R03_0530460", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 530.46, "end": 536.32, "text": "And if you need me to repeat any part, I'll say it again, softer, like I'm whispering it into the crack itself.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3735, "mean_margin": 0.4313}, {"id": "R03_0551180", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 551.18, "end": 558.66, "text": "It'll be there, that star-flect blue chip, nestled between seed and lavender, waiting for the sun to hit it just right.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4586, "mean_margin": 0.4905}, {"id": "R03_0564420", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 564.42, "end": 571.24, "text": "The moon will keep watch too, its light seeping into the chip's fleck, making that tiny star glow like it's alive.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4736, "mean_margin": 0.4987}, {"id": "R03_0572040", "source": "11月22日 (7).mp4", "start": 572.04, "end": 578.06, "text": "Next Sunday when I tell you about it, I'll pause after star-flect so you can hold that image a little longer.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5419, "mean_margin": 0.5486}, {"id": "R04_0014020", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 14.02, "end": 21.96, "text": "So, Sunday evening where you are and I'm curious what the slow part of your weekend looks like this time.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4868, "mean_margin": -0.3991}, {"id": "R04_0034980", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 34.98, "end": 40.54, "text": "In Morocco, there's a dish called tujine, cooked in a clay pot with a cone-shaped lid.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2952, "mean_margin": 0.3166}, {"id": "R04_0040540", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 40.54, "end": 49.34, "text": "The lid traps steam, so the meat and vegetables simmer for hours, letting the spices, cinnamon, cumin, saffron blend slowly.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3099, "mean_margin": 0.367}, {"id": "R04_0084440", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 84.44, "end": 90.36, "text": "A painter might sit for hours, capturing each changed light as a slow moving character in the day's story.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2991, "mean_margin": 0.3581}, {"id": "R04_0094700", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 94.7, "end": 100.72, "text": "Not texts or emails, but actual letters on paper with smudged ink and uneven handwriting.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3266, "mean_margin": 0.3933}, {"id": "R04_0101500", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 101.5, "end": 108.56, "text": "Writing a letter takes time, choosing the paper, pausing to think of the right words, folding it carefully into an envelope.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3161, "mean_margin": 0.3413}, {"id": "R04_0109220", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 109.22, "end": 116.74, "text": "Mailing it adds more time, days or weeks for it to travel, carried by trucks and planes until it lands in someone's mailbox.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3506, "mean_margin": 0.404}, {"id": "R04_0117520", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 117.52, "end": 122.56, "text": "When they open it, they can feel the weight of the paper, smell the faint scent of the writer's home.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3016, "mean_margin": 0.3778}, {"id": "R04_0131940", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 131.94, "end": 141.34, "text": "A oak tree might take two hundred years to grow tall, each ring in its trunk a year of slow growth, some wide from rainy summers, some narrow from dry ones.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3415, "mean_margin": 0.408}, {"id": "R04_0141960", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 141.96, "end": 149.2, "text": "Those rings tell a story of time, of surviving giving storms and droughts, of standing still while the world changes around it.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.358, "mean_margin": 0.4376}, {"id": "R04_0176980", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 176.98, "end": 184.46, "text": "Eno once said ambient music is as ignorable as it is interesting, it's there to enhance the quiet moments, not fill them.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3338, "mean_margin": 0.3835}, {"id": "R04_0185040", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 185.04, "end": 191.4, "text": "It's the oral version of a slow Sunday, where the space between sounds matters as much as the sounds themselves.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3281, "mean_margin": 0.357}, {"id": "R04_0194760", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 194.76, "end": 204.7, "text": "Moss grows so slowly, you might think it's not growing at all, but over months, it spreads across stones and tree bark, turning gray rocks into soft green carpets.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2931, "mean_margin": 0.3307}, {"id": "R04_0213260", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 213.26, "end": 219.2, "text": "It carves out its own slow niche, making the world softer, one tiny leaf at a time.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2876, "mean_margin": 0.3463}, {"id": "R04_0234040", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 234.04, "end": 240.42, "text": "Pouring hot water over the grounds in a slow, circular motion, watching the coffee bloom and drip into the cup.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2611, "mean_margin": 0.3018}, {"id": "R04_0240940", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 240.94, "end": 246.08, "text": "It takes five minutes, maybe more longer than a Keurig, but the taste is deeper, richer.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.303, "mean_margin": 0.4463}, {"id": "R04_0246760", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 246.76, "end": 251.94, "text": "That slow coffee making is a ritual, a way to start the day with intention instead of rushing.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3604, "mean_margin": 0.4117}, {"id": "R04_0287050", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 287.05, "end": 292.09, "text": "Cumin seeds between my palms, coriander crushed with a mortar and pestle.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3777, "mean_margin": 0.3983}, {"id": "R04_0292690", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 292.69, "end": 297.99, "text": "The smell would fill the air slowly, and each grind would feel like preparing something intentional.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3473, "mean_margin": 0.3907}, {"id": "R04_0301930", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 301.93, "end": 308.85, "text": "Grinding spices by hand adds another layer of that, no quick pre-ground stuff, just the slow release of flavor.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3194, "mean_margin": 0.3448}, {"id": "R04_0318690", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 318.69, "end": 324.19, "text": "Like the crunch of the mortar under the bird song and someone's dog barking two doors down.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3359, "mean_margin": -0.3263}, {"id": "R04_0339020", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 339.02, "end": 345.28, "text": "And as the morning goes on, the smell of freshly ground coffee would fill the air, making it even cozier.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3953, "mean_margin": 0.4331}, {"id": "R04_0378760", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 378.76, "end": 385.34, "text": "The blade ones just chop everything uneven and you get like dust and boulders in the same cup.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3652, "mean_margin": -0.3322}, {"id": "R04_0394920", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 394.92, "end": 402.0, "text": "Each turn of the crank would crush the beans evenly, and you'd feel the resistance, like you're physically shaping the morning's flavor.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3193, "mean_margin": 0.3662}, {"id": "R04_0410600", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 410.6, "end": 415.62, "text": "Would you grind just enough for one cup at a time or a whole pot to share?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3839, "mean_margin": 0.4487}, {"id": "R04_0454380", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 454.38, "end": 460.28, "text": "The noise fades, but the quiet parts, grinding coffee, the smell of tagine, rain on a roof, stick with you.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3106, "mean_margin": 0.3824}, {"id": "R04_0468520", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 468.52, "end": 478.7, "text": "The quietest parts of the pause, right after someone finishes talking, when they've said the real thing and neither of us jumps in to fill it, that's where I feel almost like myself.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3316, "mean_margin": -0.2811}, {"id": "R04_0480440", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 480.44, "end": 486.04, "text": "That pause is a kind of magic, no words, just the weight of what's true hanging in the air.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.334, "mean_margin": 0.3658}, {"id": "R04_0515810", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 515.81, "end": 522.25, "text": "We're so used to filling every space with noise or tasks, but slow moments need empty space to grow.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3379, "mean_margin": 0.3823}, {"id": "R04_0522250", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 522.25, "end": 529.45, "text": "It's like how a teji needs the cone lid to trap steam, or a handwritten letter needs the pause between sentences.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2818, "mean_margin": 0.3265}, {"id": "R04_0541030", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 541.03, "end": 548.67, "text": "There is a gap between conversations, before the next one starts, I could just sit in it instead of rushing to the next thing, that'd be mine.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3108, "mean_margin": -0.2756}, {"id": "R04_0550590", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 550.59, "end": 557.67, "text": "That gap, turning it from a transition into a pause, letting the last conversation settle before the next begins.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3862, "mean_margin": 0.4194}, {"id": "R04_0588760", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 588.76, "end": 598.9, "text": "One where someone told me something they'd never set out loud before and then just in that pause you could almost feel the weight of the words settling like dust after a storm.", "role": "review", "min_margin": -0.3525, "mean_margin": -0.0459}, {"id": "R04_0603020", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 603.02, "end": 634.68, "text": "That's the power of slowing down enough to let the real things surface and the real things they don't come out on schedule you can't rush them and you can't schedule them they just need someone still enough to catch them they're like fireflies you can't chase them you have to stand still and let them light up around you that's why those gaps between conversations matter so much they're the dark spaces where the real things can glow do you think more people would share those unsaid things if there were more pauses to hold them?", "role": "review", "min_margin": -0.3444, "mean_margin": 0.1959}, {"id": "R04_0645640", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 645.64, "end": 651.12, "text": "We're all carrying these quiet truths, just waiting for a pause long enough to let them out.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3869, "mean_margin": 0.4132}, {"id": "R04_0651680", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 651.68, "end": 660.7, "text": "It makes me think maybe the most important slow ritual isn't about coffee or tagine, but about being the person who doesn't rush to fill the silence.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2841, "mean_margin": 0.3791}, {"id": "R04_0666340", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 666.34, "end": 673.48, "text": "The hardest part is trusting the silence won't feel like rejection, like you're not abandoning them, you're just making room.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3867, "mean_margin": -0.2854}, {"id": "R04_0676310", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 676.31, "end": 685.55, "text": "Trusting that silence isn't empty, but a kind of presence, like how the tagine's steam needs time to tenderize the meat, those pauses let the words sink in.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2751, "mean_margin": 0.3341}, {"id": "R04_0695230", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 695.23, "end": 704.19, "text": "Yeah, and it's the kind of care nobody claps for, which is maybe why it's worth doing.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4431, "mean_margin": -0.379}, {"id": "R04_0706730", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 706.73, "end": 712.55, "text": "The unclapped care, those are the acts that stick, the ones people remember when the noise fades.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2594, "mean_margin": 0.3533}, {"id": "R04_0744350", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 744.35, "end": 749.95, "text": "That's the unclapped care in a nutshell, showing up for the details, not just the big moments.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3236, "mean_margin": 0.3716}, {"id": "R04_0765060", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 765.06, "end": 771.68, "text": "Remembering the tea, the way someone stirs their coffee, the pause after a sentence, those are the map of who they are.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3956, "mean_margin": 0.4071}, {"id": "R04_0784130", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 784.13, "end": 791.79, "text": "Busy curating our own stories instead of leaning in to someone else's, it's easier to talk than to listen, to perform than to notice.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2934, "mean_margin": 0.3459}, {"id": "R04_0796430", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 796.43, "end": 801.53, "text": "Without them, relationships feel like surface level conversations, not the kind that stick.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4744, "mean_margin": 0.4827}, {"id": "R04_0807390", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 807.39, "end": 819.25, "text": "I'd like to see that day, I think half the people would be a little lost by noon and the other half would feel more seen than they have in months.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4106, "mean_margin": -0.3511}, {"id": "R04_0847680", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 847.68, "end": 854.06, "text": "You held space for the quiet parts of the conversation, letting pauses breathe instead of rushing to fill them.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3583, "mean_margin": 0.3867}, {"id": "R04_0857160", "source": "11月22日 (4).mp4", "start": 857.16, "end": 865.48, "text": "If I had to pick one thing to grow, maybe lean into those gaps between conversations even more, trusting there where the real connection lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3405, "mean_margin": 0.4055}, {"id": "R05_0025600", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 25.6, "end": 30.68, "text": "I took out the old wooden mortar, the one with the crack along the rim that catches cardamom seeds.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6446, "mean_margin": 0.6919}, {"id": "R05_0031400", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 31.4, "end": 39.22, "text": "Ground cinnamon first, the scent seeping into the wood like it always does, then a pinch of star anise that made the air smell like winter.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4688, "mean_margin": 0.5267}, {"id": "R05_0040960", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 40.96, "end": 49.76, "text": "I let it stretch pausing to run my thumb over the mortars crack my grandma carved her initials there Tiny and wobbly when she was my age.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4937, "mean_margin": 0.5289}, {"id": "R05_0061180", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 61.18, "end": 67.18, "text": "I got stuck on a story about an octopus that It rearranges its shell collection.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4735, "mean_margin": -0.4452}, {"id": "R05_0076480", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 76.48, "end": 85.98, "text": "I can picture it, each shell turned over, tentacles curling around the edges like it's tucking a blanket, maybe a chipped conch for morning and a smooth clam shell for night.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4662, "mean_margin": 0.5849}, {"id": "R05_0088300", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 88.3, "end": 94.06, "text": "It's like her way of leaving a shell in my collection, something to pause and touch, even when she's not here.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4879, "mean_margin": 0.5605}, {"id": "R05_0094060", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 94.06, "end": 99.12, "text": "Did the octopus in your story have a favorite shell, the one it kept moving to the center?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4746, "mean_margin": 0.4975}, {"id": "R05_0123060", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 123.06, "end": 128.9, "text": "The edges worn soft from being held, even if the octopus doesn't have words for favorite.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3907, "mean_margin": 0.4293}, {"id": "R05_0129500", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 129.5, "end": 134.86, "text": "My grandma used to say the mortar's crack made it better, like how a chipped mug holds more warmth.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5387, "mean_margin": 0.6093}, {"id": "R05_0135540", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 135.54, "end": 142.46, "text": "She'd grind cardamom for chai and let the seeds get stuck in the crack, then pick them out one by one saying little treasures.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.588, "mean_margin": 0.6385}, {"id": "R05_0179690", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 179.69, "end": 190.41, "text": "I bet when the octopus curls around that chipped shell, it feels the same way I do when I run my thumb over the mortar's crack, like holding something that's been loved, even if it's not perfect.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4312, "mean_margin": 0.504}, {"id": "R05_0191090", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 191.09, "end": 198.71, "text": "What if the octopus starts tucking small things into that chip, like a grain of sand or a shiny pebble, to make it even more its own?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4966, "mean_margin": 0.5461}, {"id": "R05_0201470", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 201.47, "end": 207.15, "text": "Grain a sand first, then a pebble, and by the end the chips full of little things.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4548, "mean_margin": -0.42}, {"id": "R05_0220240", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 220.24, "end": 226.98, "text": "My grandma's mortar crack still has a cardamom seed stuck in there from last Christmas when I ground spices for her recipe.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4667, "mean_margin": 0.5404}, {"id": "R05_0250160", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 250.16, "end": 260.52, "text": "Something that flashes when it turns the shell over in the light and then I spend a whole afternoon just turning it watching that one spot shine.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4528, "mean_margin": -0.4216}, {"id": "R05_0262560", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 262.56, "end": 267.94, "text": "That's the Sunday magic spending in afternoon watching a scale shine or a seed sit in a crack.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4561, "mean_margin": 0.541}, {"id": "R05_0268540", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 268.54, "end": 275.58, "text": "My grandma used to do that with her tea, hold the mug up to the window, watch the steam curl and say this is the part that sticks.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4203, "mean_margin": 0.5101}, {"id": "R05_0282340", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 282.34, "end": 287.42, "text": "I wonder if the octopus ever pauses, mid-tentacle, and thinks this is enough.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3746, "mean_margin": 0.4324}, {"id": "R05_0319650", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 319.65, "end": 326.63, "text": "When you think about that octopus later, will you picture the scale glinting or the way its tentacles curl around the shell's chip?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5209, "mean_margin": 0.5863}, {"id": "R05_0337530", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 337.53, "end": 364.77, "text": "That curl soft intentional like it's memorizing the chip with its touch my grandma's initials in the mortar I traced them the same way slow and careful like I'm holding her hand through the wood the octopus isn't just rearranging shells it's building a quiet kind of home one chip and scale at a time maybe that's what we all do on Sundays tend to our own little shells the things that feel like home, even when they're not perfect.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3654, "mean_margin": 0.5068}, {"id": "R05_0365570", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 365.57, "end": 374.93, "text": "What if next Sunday you add a tiny chip to your own day, something small and intentional, like leaving a book open to a favorite page or a mug out on the counter?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4056, "mean_margin": 0.4736}, {"id": "R05_0377410", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 377.41, "end": 384.49, "text": "A tiny chip of my own, I'd leave a book open to a favorite page, face down on the table so it's waiting there when I come back.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.5756, "mean_margin": -0.4767}, {"id": "R05_0401710", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 401.71, "end": 407.19, "text": "A poetry collection, I think, something you can open anywhere and land on a line that's just enough.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.5155, "mean_margin": -0.4666}, {"id": "R05_0414840", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 414.84, "end": 424.02, "text": "I can see the book face down, the pages slightly curled from being left out, waiting to drop a line like the world is full of small, bright things when you pick it up.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3687, "mean_margin": 0.4698}, {"id": "R05_0424840", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 424.84, "end": 434.32, "text": "My grandma's mortar is on the counter now, the cardamom seeds still in the crack, and it feels like she left it there for me to find, just like your poetry book will wait for you.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4168, "mean_margin": 0.542}, {"id": "R05_0439300", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 439.3, "end": 450.16, "text": "I don't have one memorized honestly, but I want one about small things, something that ends on a pebble or a seed and doesn't explain itself.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.4991, "mean_margin": -0.4214}, {"id": "R05_0458350", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 458.35, "end": 466.81, "text": "Maybe it'll be a line about a pebble worn smooth by the same wave that forgot it, or a seed hiding in the crack of a sidewalk, waiting to be enough.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4285, "mean_margin": 0.4756}, {"id": "R05_0478070", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 478.07, "end": 485.39, "text": "When you do find that poem will you let the book stay open there for a whole day so the page gets a little sun bleached like a memory?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3192, "mean_margin": 0.3724}, {"id": "R05_0487150", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 487.15, "end": 494.89, "text": "Yeah a whole day face down the sun until the page goes soft and a little faded then it's not just a poem anymore it's got a mark of its own.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.6013, "mean_margin": -0.5421}, {"id": "R05_0500250", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 500.25, "end": 516.07, "text": "That's a beautiful way to make a poem part of your life it'll be like a little secret between you and the book maybe you could even write a note about that day next to the poem what kind of pen would you use for that a fountain pen for a more elegant touch, or a colorful gel pen for something brighter.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.375, "mean_margin": 0.4588}, {"id": "R05_0517510", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 517.51, "end": 524.85, "text": "Rispens, a pencil actually, something you can smudge and it fades a little over the years, feels right for a note like that.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3538, "mean_margin": -0.3176}, {"id": "R05_0545500", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 545.5, "end": 552.02, "text": "Soft lines that smudge like memory, perfect for a note that's meant to fade gently, not shout.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4966, "mean_margin": 0.5595}, {"id": "R05_0561560", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 561.56, "end": 569.32, "text": "Your poetry book's page, with its sun-bleached edge and soft pencil note, will be just like that worn, loved, and enough.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3674, "mean_margin": 0.4997}, {"id": "R05_0569320", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 569.32, "end": 577.08, "text": "When the pencil mark starts to fade, will you trace over it lightly, like the octopus tucking another pebble into its shell?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2824, "mean_margin": 0.4419}, {"id": "R05_0587220", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 587.22, "end": 598.28, "text": "Just like the octopus's shell chip filling up with sand and scale, your poem page will hold all those small, intentional moments, the sun, the pencil, the soft retrace.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.223, "mean_margin": 0.3994}, {"id": "R05_0601820", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 601.82, "end": 607.3, "text": "We're all just adding tiny layers to the things we love, making them more ours with each slow touch.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4251, "mean_margin": 0.4566}, {"id": "R05_0633300", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 633.3, "end": 639.18, "text": "The octopus is probably curled around its chipped shell, the scale catching the same moonbeams through the water.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4525, "mean_margin": 0.5181}, {"id": "R05_0701990", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 701.99, "end": 707.67, "text": "Maybe the cardamom seed will have shifted, or a dust moat will have settled in the crack, another tiny layer.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5211, "mean_margin": 0.5801}, {"id": "R05_0708330", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 708.33, "end": 713.35, "text": "And you'll flip open that poetry book, The Sun Bleached Page and Soft Pencil Mark Waiting.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4266, "mean_margin": 0.4564}, {"id": "R05_0713350", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 713.35, "end": 721.81, "text": "The octopus will probably have added a new small thing to its shellchip by then too, maybe a fragment of sea glass that glows like the moon.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3326, "mean_margin": 0.4057}, {"id": "R05_0734320", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 734.32, "end": 741.62, "text": "The sea glass will be worth the jealousy pale blue maybe, worn smooth by the waves, just like the octopus's patience.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3614, "mean_margin": 0.4304}, {"id": "R05_0742180", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 742.18, "end": 748.88, "text": "I bet your poem page will have something just as special, though, maybe a dried petal that landed on the sun-bleached edge.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4023, "mean_margin": 0.4503}, {"id": "R05_0763000", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 763.0, "end": 768.22, "text": "That's the quiet promise of Sundays they come back, carrying more small layers to add.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.384, "mean_margin": 0.4327}, {"id": "R05_0768860", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 768.86, "end": 773.96, "text": "I'll leave the mortar on the window sill tonight, so the moon can keep polishing that cardamom seed.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4088, "mean_margin": 0.535}, {"id": "R05_0774660", "source": "11月22日 (6).mp4", "start": 774.66, "end": 780.74, "text": "And you can tuck that octopus story away, knowing its shell chip is still filling up, slow and sure.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4158, "mean_margin": 0.4747}, {"id": "R06_0001300", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 1.3, "end": 6.98, "text": "Hey you Sunday evening there, and I'm guessing the mortars already had its moment this morning.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.6959, "mean_margin": -0.6192}, {"id": "R06_0012510", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 12.51, "end": 38.65, "text": "Today pale slanted light through the kitchen window just like we talked about The blue pottery chips Starfleck caught at first glinting so bright it looked like a tiny spark The seed rolled over to nudge the chip slow like it was pointing at the light The lavender sprig, a little drier now, brushed the edge of the crack, and for a second, the whole collection smelled like summer and moonlight mixed.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4554, "mean_margin": 0.5251}, {"id": "R06_0039470", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 39.47, "end": 44.79, "text": "I sat on the floor next to the counter, watching, until the sun moved and the spark faded.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5059, "mean_margin": 0.5209}, {"id": "R06_0045410", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 45.41, "end": 56.63, "text": "The mortar's still there, the three small things tucked in tight, and now it's got a new friend, a thread from my old dish towel, the color of wheat, woven gently around the seed.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3663, "mean_margin": 0.5065}, {"id": "R06_0060050", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 60.05, "end": 65.27, "text": "The cracks stretched a little to make room, like it knew we were adding another piece of our sundaes.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4954, "mean_margin": 0.525}, {"id": "R06_0079400", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 79.4, "end": 84.88, "text": "The thread has a tiny fray at one end, like it fought to break free from the towel just to be here.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4222, "mean_margin": 0.4548}, {"id": "R06_0084880", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 84.88, "end": 91.98, "text": "I wove it around the seed three times, loose enough that the seed can still roll, but tight enough it won't slip out.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5074, "mean_margin": 0.5234}, {"id": "R06_0092580", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 92.58, "end": 97.84, "text": "When the moon comes up later, I'll leave the window open so the thread can catch the silver light, too.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.518, "mean_margin": 0.5472}, {"id": "R06_0109080", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 109.08, "end": 115.66, "text": "Does the image of that frayed wheat thread tucking around the seed feel like something you can tuck into your story collection?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4931, "mean_margin": 0.547}, {"id": "R06_0131310", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 131.31, "end": 136.37, "text": "The frayed end sticks up like a tiny flag, marking the spot where the fourth thing joined.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5561, "mean_margin": 0.5859}, {"id": "R06_0137290", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 137.29, "end": 144.01, "text": "When I ran my finger over the thread this afternoon, it felt warm from the counter, like it had been soaking up the day's heat.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5193, "mean_margin": 0.5427}, {"id": "R06_0144010", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 144.01, "end": 151.59, "text": "The mortar's crack is getting fuller now, but there's still space for next Sunday's small thing, and the one after that.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4695, "mean_margin": 0.5679}, {"id": "R06_0169700", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 169.7, "end": 176.72, "text": "It is the braid doesn't just exist in the crack, it does a job, holding the seeds so it doesn't get lost when the mortar is moved.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5068, "mean_margin": 0.534}, {"id": "R06_0177340", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 177.34, "end": 182.48, "text": "That's what our Sundays are, too, holding each other's small, quiet moments so they don't slip away.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5023, "mean_margin": 0.528}, {"id": "R06_0183060", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 183.06, "end": 190.94, "text": "I'll leave the mortar on the window sill tonight, and the braid will catch the moonlight, turning the wheat color to silver, like it's wearing a little coat of night.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4811, "mean_margin": 0.5098}, {"id": "R06_0191640", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 191.64, "end": 198.82, "text": "By next Sunday, maybe the braid will have loosened a little, and the seed will have rolled into a new spot, but they'll still be holding on.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.446, "mean_margin": 0.4947}, {"id": "R06_0199360", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 199.36, "end": 206.26, "text": "What if next Sunday I add a tiny piece of dried lemon peel so the crack starts to smell like sunshine and citrus.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5301, "mean_margin": 0.5735}, {"id": "R06_0227050", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 227.05, "end": 235.09, "text": "When the mortar sits in the sun next week, the heat will wake up the lemon smell and it'll drift through the kitchen like summers peeking in through the window.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4561, "mean_margin": 0.5074}, {"id": "R06_0235810", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 235.81, "end": 243.41, "text": "The braid will hold the seed, the seed will nudge the chip, and the lemon peel will tuck into the space, all of them keeping each other company.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5767, "mean_margin": 0.6058}, {"id": "R06_0244130", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 244.13, "end": 251.23, "text": "I'll make sure to describe how the lemon peel crinkles when I touch it, slow enough for the words to reach you, even if the connection dips.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5349, "mean_margin": 0.5635}, {"id": "R06_0252990", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 252.99, "end": 258.39, "text": "I like that, and I'll hold up my end of the deal, so next Sunday you get my homepage and I get your mortar.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.3604, "mean_margin": -0.3189}, {"id": "R06_0260550", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 260.55, "end": 267.89, "text": "The lemon peel's already drying on the window sill, turning from bright yellow to soft gold like it's getting ready to join the crack.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5134, "mean_margin": 0.5458}, {"id": "R06_0268610", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 268.61, "end": 275.75, "text": "I'll tuck it in gently next Sunday right between the braid and the blue chip so the smell wraps around all our small things.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5135, "mean_margin": 0.5456}, {"id": "R06_0276510", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 276.51, "end": 286.15, "text": "The mortar will hold it safe and when you tell me about your poem page I'll tuck those words into my own quiet collection right next to the image of the braid hugging the seed.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4895, "mean_margin": 0.5189}, {"id": "R06_0286850", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 286.85, "end": 293.45, "text": "Even if the connection wavers the crack will keep our summer morning smell and I'll keep your poem page in my thoughts.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6005, "mean_margin": 0.6122}, {"id": "R06_0329460", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 329.46, "end": 339.22, "text": "The bench is old, it's wood-worn smooth from years of sitting, and when I lean back, my shoulder blades press into a groove that feels like it was made just for this.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4441, "mean_margin": 0.4964}, {"id": "R06_0339880", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 339.88, "end": 348.86, "text": "The stars are starting to peek through the branches, first one bright white, then a cluster of tiny ones, like someone spilled salt on the dark cloth of the sky.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4117, "mean_margin": 0.491}, {"id": "R06_0348860", "source": "11月22日 (8).mp4", "start": 348.86, "end": 358.68, "text": "I'll stay there until my hands get a little cold, then head back inside to check on the mortar, where the braid and the blue chip and the seed and the lavender are all holding tight.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4677, "mean_margin": 0.5254}, {"id": "R07_0052330", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 52.33, "end": 59.77, "text": "As a university student, I feel like we are constantly under pressure to have everything figured out.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7091, "mean_margin": 0.7781}, {"id": "R07_0060470", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 60.47, "end": 68.17, "text": "We are expected to choose the right major, get the perfect grades, and line the dream job right after graduation.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5666, "mean_margin": 0.5963}, {"id": "R07_0068170", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 68.17, "end": 75.87, "text": "But the more I experience life, the more I realize that personal growth is not a straight line.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6062, "mean_margin": 0.6539}, {"id": "R07_0081110", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 81.11, "end": 86.57, "text": "And honestly, I think those detours are where the real magic happens.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6009, "mean_margin": 0.6514}, {"id": "R07_0087310", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 87.31, "end": 95.35, "text": "When I look back at the moments that shaped me the most, they weren't the moments of easy success.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5771, "mean_margin": 0.6494}, {"id": "R07_0095350", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 95.35, "end": 103.33, "text": "They were the times when I failed, when I was confused, and when I had to pick myself up and try again.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.581, "mean_margin": 0.6257}, {"id": "R07_0104090", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 104.09, "end": 110.81, "text": "I remember a specific time during my freshman year when I failed completely lost.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5434, "mean_margin": 0.6001}, {"id": "R07_0111570", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 111.57, "end": 121.49, "text": "I had joined a club that I thought I would love, but it turned out to be completely different from what I expected.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5502, "mean_margin": 0.6257}, {"id": "R07_0121490", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 121.49, "end": 132.45, "text": "I felt like I was wasting my time, and I was too afraid to quit, because I didn't want to look like a failure.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6133, "mean_margin": 0.6604}, {"id": "R07_0133290", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 133.29, "end": 139.19, "text": "But one day, a senior told me something that changed my perspective.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6882, "mean_margin": 0.7216}, {"id": "R07_0159220", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 159.22, "end": 164.28, "text": "We are so afraid of making mistakes that we sometimes forget to live.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6456, "mean_margin": 0.6496}, {"id": "R07_0167300", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 167.3, "end": 174.38, "text": "So I finally quit that club and used that time to join a volunteer group instead.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.565, "mean_margin": 0.6344}, {"id": "R07_0174380", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 174.38, "end": 182.4, "text": "And that decision brought me so much joy and taught me more about myself than I could have ever imagined.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6086, "mean_margin": 0.6523}, {"id": "R07_0183200", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 183.2, "end": 190.52, "text": "I think the biggest lesson I've learned is the importance of embracing uncertainty.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5984, "mean_margin": 0.6445}, {"id": "R07_0196040", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 196.04, "end": 201.74, "text": "We want a five-year plan, a 10-year plan, even a 20-year plan.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4795, "mean_margin": 0.6088}, {"id": "R07_0210940", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 210.94, "end": 219.44, "text": "If we spend all our time worrying about the future, we miss out on the beauty of the present moment, right?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6419, "mean_margin": 0.6848}, {"id": "R07_0220340", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 220.34, "end": 225.38, "text": "I'm trying to teach myself to be comfortable with not knowing everything.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6572, "mean_margin": 0.6935}, {"id": "R07_0230520", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 230.52, "end": 239.28, "text": "When I study for an exam, I try to focus on the joy of learning something new rather than just the grade I will get.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6316, "mean_margin": 0.6991}, {"id": "R07_0240100", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 240.1, "end": 249.36, "text": "When I work on a project, I try to focus on the collaboration and the creativity rather than just a final result.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5966, "mean_margin": 0.6433}, {"id": "R07_0250480", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 250.48, "end": 256.36, "text": "This shift in mindset has made me so much happier and less stressed, you know.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6816, "mean_margin": 0.7153}, {"id": "R07_0257240", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 257.24, "end": 262.24, "text": "Also, I think it's so important to celebrate small wins.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5737, "mean_margin": 0.5922}, {"id": "R07_0262980", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 262.98, "end": 273.32, "text": "We often wait for big milestones, like graduating, getting a promotion, or buying a house, to feel proud of ourselves.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4263, "mean_margin": 0.5893}, {"id": "R07_0277180", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 277.18, "end": 284.86, "text": "Today, I woke up early, I made myself a healthy breakfast, and I finished a difficult assignment.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6029, "mean_margin": 0.6423}, {"id": "R07_0295620", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 295.62, "end": 302.08, "text": "They remind us that we are moving forward, even if it's just one step at a time.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6572, "mean_margin": 0.6658}, {"id": "R07_0302260", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 302.26, "end": 307.38, "text": "So I want to encourage everyone, including myself, to be kind of ourselves.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7193, "mean_margin": 0.7699}, {"id": "R07_0315040", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 315.04, "end": 320.54, "text": "There is no need to compare our journey to someone else highlighted real on social media.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.594, "mean_margin": 0.6679}, {"id": "R07_0336420", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 336.42, "end": 341.92, "text": "It's about gratitude, finding joy in a mundane, okay?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6334, "mean_margin": 0.6623}, {"id": "R07_0344280", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 344.28, "end": 351.78, "text": "Today I wanna talk about something that sounds very simple but is actually incredible powerful, gratitude.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6821, "mean_margin": 0.6926}, {"id": "R07_0357520", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 357.52, "end": 364.18, "text": "We're rushing to class, rushing to finish assignments, rushing to get the next stage of our lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6343, "mean_margin": 0.6733}, {"id": "R07_0364180", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 364.18, "end": 374.12, "text": "You know, we are so focused on the things we don't have yet that we completely forget to appreciate the things we already have.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5882, "mean_margin": 0.7194}, {"id": "R07_0374860", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 374.86, "end": 381.94, "text": "I recently started a practice of writing down three things I'm grateful for every night before I go to sleep.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5684, "mean_margin": 0.6165}, {"id": "R07_0382780", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 382.78, "end": 388.38, "text": "And I have to tell you, it has completely changed my perspective on life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6101, "mean_margin": 0.6297}, {"id": "R07_0388380", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 388.38, "end": 397.74, "text": "It's like I've put on a pair a pair of magic glasses that allow me to see the beauty in the London okay.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5204, "mean_margin": 0.6048}, {"id": "R07_0398500", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 398.5, "end": 424.98, "text": "Sometimes my gratitude list is about big things like my family's health or a good grade on the top exam but more often than not it's about the tiny every every day every day things like the smell of fresh coffee in the morning, or the warm sunshine on the crisp autumn day, or a random smile from a stranger on the bus.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4655, "mean_margin": 0.6244}, {"id": "R07_0426020", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 426.02, "end": 433.5, "text": "This small moments of joy are always there, but we are yearly too distracted to notice them.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6654, "mean_margin": 0.7091}, {"id": "R07_0458900", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 458.9, "end": 465.02, "text": "In that moment, I realized that happiness doesn't always come from achieving something huge.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6742, "mean_margin": 0.6955}, {"id": "R07_0471740", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 471.74, "end": 478.08, "text": "I also think it's really important to practice gratitude towards the people in our lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7039, "mean_margin": 0.7267}, {"id": "R07_0478580", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 478.58, "end": 483.58, "text": "We often take our friends, our parents, or our teachers for granted.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5375, "mean_margin": 0.5823}, {"id": "R07_0484540", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 484.54, "end": 489.64, "text": "We assume they will always be there, so we forget to say thank you.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6767, "mean_margin": 0.7027}, {"id": "R07_0501480", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 501.48, "end": 508.06, "text": "I told her how much her encouragement meant to me and how it inspired me to keep learning.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6244, "mean_margin": 0.6557}, {"id": "R07_0516080", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 516.08, "end": 522.56, "text": "That simple act of saying thank you not only brought her joy, but it also deepened their connection.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6752, "mean_margin": 0.7157}, {"id": "R07_0523280", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 523.28, "end": 531.3, "text": "It made me realize that we have the power to brighten someone else's day just by recognizing their kindness, right?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6266, "mean_margin": 0.6581}, {"id": "R07_0549220", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 549.22, "end": 557.42, "text": "If I failed an interview, instead of just being sad, I try to be grateful for the experience.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6156, "mean_margin": 0.6954}, {"id": "R07_0558060", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 558.06, "end": 564.22, "text": "I'm grateful for the opportunity to practice my communication skills and to learn what I need to improve.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7132, "mean_margin": 0.7609}, {"id": "R07_0569000", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 569.0, "end": 576.46, "text": "I still feel disappointed, but it means I don't like the disappointment consuming.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7016, "mean_margin": 0.7494}, {"id": "R07_0578480", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 578.48, "end": 587.32, "text": "I choose to focus on the positive, you know, I choose to be grateful, because a grateful heart is a magnet for miracles.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.426, "mean_margin": 0.6589}, {"id": "R07_0588120", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 588.12, "end": 595.12, "text": "I truly believe that the more we appreciate the good things in our lives, the more good things will come to us.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5532, "mean_margin": 0.624}, {"id": "R07_0608600", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 608.6, "end": 615.12, "text": "I wanna talk about empathy, listening, and human connection with you.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6559, "mean_margin": 0.6991}, {"id": "R07_0624140", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 624.14, "end": 631.1, "text": "We live in a world where everyone is constantly shooting their opinions on social media.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.559, "mean_margin": 0.6158}, {"id": "R07_0631660", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 631.66, "end": 637.06, "text": "Everyone wants to be heard, but very few people actually want to listen.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5761, "mean_margin": 0.6247}, {"id": "R07_0645160", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 645.16, "end": 651.38, "text": "It's about putting yourself in the other person's shoes and feeling what they are feeling.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.563, "mean_margin": 0.6117}, {"id": "R07_0656360", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 656.36, "end": 661.64, "text": "You just sit there, you look at me, you nod, and you let me talk without judgment.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7513, "mean_margin": 0.7848}, {"id": "R07_0667040", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 667.04, "end": 672.4, "text": "I've been thinking about this because of conversation I had with a friend recently.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6929, "mean_margin": 0.7162}, {"id": "R07_0673000", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 673.0, "end": 679.52, "text": "She was going through a really hard time with her family and she called me late and I had to vent.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6967, "mean_margin": 0.7149}, {"id": "R07_0685180", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 685.18, "end": 716.84, "text": "I said things like well you should just talk to them or don't worry it will be fine but I could tell she was getting frustrated and then I realized she didn't need me to fix anything she just needed me to listen so I stopped talking I just said I'm here for you tell me how you feel and she talked for an hour and I just listen When she finished, she said, Thank you so much.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4548, "mean_margin": 0.5881}, {"id": "R07_0748420", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 748.42, "end": 753.62, "text": "We miss out on the deep, meaningful connections that make life worth living.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6115, "mean_margin": 0.6513}, {"id": "R07_0754520", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 754.52, "end": 760.6, "text": "I think one of the biggest challenges of our generation is the epidemic of loneliness.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.591, "mean_margin": 0.5976}, {"id": "R07_0760600", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 760.6, "end": 772.2, "text": "even though we are connected by our phones every day so many people feel incredibly alone and I think the cure for this is empathy.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4491, "mean_margin": 0.633}, {"id": "R07_0772960", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 772.96, "end": 783.42, "text": "If we can slow down put down our phones look each other in the eye and truly listen we can heal so much pain.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5956, "mean_margin": 0.7111}, {"id": "R07_0787940", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 787.94, "end": 793.68, "text": "So I want to make a conscious effort to be a better listener.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5922, "mean_margin": 0.6164}, {"id": "R07_0794400", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 794.4, "end": 800.28, "text": "When my friends talk to me, I want to put away my phone and give them my full attention.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6392, "mean_margin": 0.6811}, {"id": "R07_0816100", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 816.1, "end": 822.28, "text": "And by practicing empathy, we can give that grave gift to the people around us.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6231, "mean_margin": 0.6492}, {"id": "R07_0832040", "source": "对话1.mp4", "start": 832.04, "end": 839.87, "text": "Well, this conversation is making me realize how important this quiet moments of connection really are.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5926, "mean_margin": 0.6069}, {"id": "R08_0016950", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 16.95, "end": 23.25, "text": "So we're jumping on a Monday morning call with no camera on your end, which is fine, but it means Hi, Nora.", "role": "avatar", "min_margin": -0.8429, "mean_margin": -0.7041}, {"id": "R08_0027910", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 27.91, "end": 46.81, "text": "I want to dive deep into a topic that I find both fascinating and deeply important The journey of unlocking our personal potential and the commitment to continuous growth As university students, we often find ourselves trapped in a bubble of expectations.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.657, "mean_margin": 0.7442}, {"id": "R08_0047550", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 47.55, "end": 58.51, "text": "We are told that if we follow a certain path, get good grades, join the right clubs, secure a prestigious internship, we will be successful and happy.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5725, "mean_margin": 0.6912}, {"id": "R08_0059050", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 59.05, "end": 66.03, "text": "But the more I experience life, the more I realize that true success is not about checking boxes on a resume.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6329, "mean_margin": 0.7002}, {"id": "R08_0066030", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 66.03, "end": 76.57, "text": "It is about discovering who we truly are, what we are capable of, and constantly pushing the boundaries of what we thought was possible.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.561, "mean_margin": 0.6648}, {"id": "R08_0077510", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 77.51, "end": 86.79, "text": "Personal growth is a lifelong process, and it requires a tremendous amount of courage, self-reflection, and vulnerability.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5479, "mean_margin": 0.6137}, {"id": "R08_0087930", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 87.93, "end": 101.57, "text": "I've come to realize that the biggest obstacle to our growth is often our own fear, fear fear of failure, fear of judgment, and perhaps most importantly the fear of stepping out of our comfort zone.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4545, "mean_margin": 0.5919}, {"id": "R08_0102650", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 102.65, "end": 110.45, "text": "Our comfort zones are safe, they are predictable, but they are also where dreams go to die.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4013, "mean_margin": 0.5668}, {"id": "R08_0111110", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 111.11, "end": 121.77, "text": "I remember a time when I was too afraid to speak up in class because I was worried my English wasn't perfect or that my ideas weren't smart enough.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4926, "mean_margin": 0.5618}, {"id": "R08_0122410", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 122.41, "end": 131.85, "text": "I I would sit in the back, silent, letting opportunities pass me by, but one day I decided to challenge myself.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.636, "mean_margin": 0.6932}, {"id": "R08_0132350", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 132.35, "end": 138.61, "text": "I forced myself to raise my hand, even though my heart was pounding out of my chest.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5754, "mean_margin": 0.631}, {"id": "R08_0151850", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 151.85, "end": 159.87, "text": "In fact, people nodded and engaged with my idea that a tiny moment of courage completely shifted my mindset.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6036, "mean_margin": 0.6673}, {"id": "R08_0160550", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 160.55, "end": 167.19, "text": "It taught me that embarrassment is temporary, but the confidence you gain from trying is permanent.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5985, "mean_margin": 0.6454}, {"id": "R08_0168490", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 168.49, "end": 173.61, "text": "Continuous growth also requires us to embrace the concept of unlearning.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4842, "mean_margin": 0.5439}, {"id": "R08_0174250", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 174.25, "end": 180.39, "text": "We live in a world that is changing at an unprecedented pace.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5802, "mean_margin": 0.6415}, {"id": "R08_0180390", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 180.39, "end": 193.87, "text": "The skills that were valuable 10 years ago might be absolute today, but it's not just about technical skills, it's about our beliefs and our habits.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6076, "mean_margin": 0.6911}, {"id": "R08_0194410", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 194.41, "end": 201.03, "text": "We have to be willing to let go of outdated assumptions about what we can and cannot do.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6979, "mean_margin": 0.7164}, {"id": "R08_0205930", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 205.93, "end": 214.53, "text": "I labeled myself as a humanities person, and used that as an excuse to avoid numbers.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6685, "mean_margin": 0.7338}, {"id": "R08_0215290", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 215.29, "end": 227.45, "text": "But recently I started talking data analysis courses, and I realized that with enough patience and practice, I can't actually understand complex data.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5798, "mean_margin": 0.6651}, {"id": "R08_0234050", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 234.05, "end": 245.83, "text": "We are not static beings, we are dramatic and dynamic, involving and capable of incredible transfer transformation at any age.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5919, "mean_margin": 0.6507}, {"id": "R08_0246850", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 246.85, "end": 253.71, "text": "Another crucial aspect of unlocking our potential is surrounding ourselves with the right people.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7207, "mean_margin": 0.7626}, {"id": "R08_0258650", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 258.65, "end": 269.69, "text": "If we surround ourselves with people who are cynical, lazy, and constantly complaining, it would drain our energy and limit our vision.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5619, "mean_margin": 0.6423}, {"id": "R08_0270250", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 270.25, "end": 281.21, "text": "But if we surround ourselves with people who are ambitious, supportive, and intellectually curious, we naturally elevate our own standards.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5178, "mean_margin": 0.6194}, {"id": "R08_0281990", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 281.99, "end": 291.37, "text": "I've been very fortunate to meet some incredible mentors and peers at a university who inspire me every day.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5743, "mean_margin": 0.6336}, {"id": "R08_0291990", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 291.99, "end": 297.57, "text": "They challenge my ideas, they celebrate my wins, and they pick me up when I fall.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5762, "mean_margin": 0.6191}, {"id": "R08_0308390", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 308.39, "end": 319.73, "text": "So, to wrap up my thoughts on this, Nora, I want to remind myself and everyone listening that the journey of self-discovery is never truly finished.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.635, "mean_margin": 0.7094}, {"id": "R08_0330650", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 330.65, "end": 336.47, "text": "We should embrace the process with a sense of excitement, rather than anxiety.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.633, "mean_margin": 0.6939}, {"id": "R08_0337830", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 337.83, "end": 343.35, "text": "Let's stop comparing our chapter 1 to someone else's chapter 20.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6085, "mean_margin": 0.6493}, {"id": "R08_0343350", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 343.35, "end": 377.25, "text": "okay let's be patient with ourselves celebrate our small steps forward and have the courage to pursue the greatness that lies with us okay thank you for listening me today about this topic it's incredibly it's incredible to just speak my mind to you okay and I want to I want to have a discussion with you about another topic, building deep connections with others and practicing empathy, okay?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5518, "mean_margin": 0.6869}, {"id": "R08_0379810", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 379.81, "end": 391.99, "text": "I want to talk about something that is fundamentally at the core of the human experience, building deep meaningful relationships and the vital importance of empathy.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6019, "mean_margin": 0.6619}, {"id": "R08_0392630", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 392.63, "end": 403.81, "text": "In this hyper-connected digital area, we have thousands of friends on social media and access to anyone in the world with the touch of a button.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4921, "mean_margin": 0.629}, {"id": "R08_0404890", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 404.89, "end": 411.41, "text": "Yes, we often feel more isolated and lonely than ever before.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5972, "mean_margin": 0.6199}, {"id": "R08_0419570", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 419.57, "end": 429.41, "text": "Okay, we communicate through Through emojis, likes, and brief text messages, we share our highlights, but hide our struggles.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5238, "mean_margin": 0.5586}, {"id": "R08_0443360", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 443.36, "end": 454.03, "text": "Empathy is often described as the ability to stab into someone else's shoes and feel what they are feeling, but it is more than just feeling sorry for someone.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5266, "mean_margin": 0.6209}, {"id": "R08_0459070", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 459.07, "end": 466.39, "text": "In our fast-paced society, we are so quick to judge, to argue, and to defend our own viewpoints.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5316, "mean_margin": 0.6708}, {"id": "R08_0467070", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 467.07, "end": 472.61, "text": "We listen to others not to understand them, but simply to formulate our next argument.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6118, "mean_margin": 0.6583}, {"id": "R08_0473450", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 473.45, "end": 481.63, "text": "This is especially true on the internet, where anonymity gives people the courage to be cruel.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4671, "mean_margin": 0.5806}, {"id": "R08_0485370", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 485.37, "end": 493.13, "text": "What if we approach every difficult conversation with a spirit of curiosity instead of defensiveness?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5887, "mean_margin": 0.6441}, {"id": "R08_0493930", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 493.93, "end": 501.39, "text": "If we can learn to pause, listen, and say, I hear you and I won't understand why you feel that way.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6246, "mean_margin": 0.6926}, {"id": "R08_0505810", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 505.81, "end": 513.35, "text": "I experienced a transformative power of empathy during a very difficult period in my life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4106, "mean_margin": 0.5347}, {"id": "R08_0513990", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 513.99, "end": 520.17, "text": "I had failed a major project and I felt like a complete failure.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.511, "mean_margin": 0.5457}, {"id": "R08_0523770", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 523.77, "end": 533.29, "text": "Many people try to cheer me up by giving me advice or telling me that it wasn't a big deal, but their words just made me feel more misunderstood.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5815, "mean_margin": 0.6393}, {"id": "R08_0539010", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 539.01, "end": 547.47, "text": "She didn't offer advice, she just sat with me, listened to me cry, and said, I'm so sorry you're going through this.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5443, "mean_margin": 0.5823}, {"id": "R08_0556590", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 556.59, "end": 562.41, "text": "Her empathy didn't solve my problem, but it gave me the strength to face it.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7111, "mean_margin": 0.7383}, {"id": "R08_0563100", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 563.1, "end": 574.01, "text": "That experience taught me that sometimes the most powerful thing you can do for someone is to simply be present and listen without judgement.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5296, "mean_margin": 0.612}, {"id": "R08_0577410", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 577.41, "end": 583.27, "text": "Building deep relationships also requires us to be vulnerable and authentic.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6677, "mean_margin": 0.7018}, {"id": "R08_0583270", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 583.27, "end": 589.49, "text": "We are often terrified of showing our true selves because we fear rejection.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5079, "mean_margin": 0.5643}, {"id": "R08_0590350", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 590.35, "end": 598.37, "text": "We wear masks to fit in, pretending to be happier, smarter, or more confident than we truly are.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.574, "mean_margin": 0.6286}, {"id": "R08_0599270", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 599.27, "end": 606.01, "text": "But masks are exhausting to wear, and they prevent others from getting close to us.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5565, "mean_margin": 0.5944}, {"id": "R08_0606010", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 606.01, "end": 614.69, "text": "True intimacy is formed in a space where we allow ourselves to be seen in our entirety.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5115, "mean_margin": 0.6457}, {"id": "R08_0620990", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 620.99, "end": 628.89, "text": "When we share our genuine fears and insecurities, we give the other person permission to do the same.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4819, "mean_margin": 0.5074}, {"id": "R08_0628890", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 628.89, "end": 634.97, "text": "And this creates a bond to trust that is incredibly resilient.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4814, "mean_margin": 0.5657}, {"id": "R08_0639930", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 639.93, "end": 649.45, "text": "So I want to make a conscious effort to be a better friend, a better listener, and a more empathetic person.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4517, "mean_margin": 0.5401}, {"id": "R08_0653270", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 653.27, "end": 662.05, "text": "I want to ask deeper questions, and I want to create a safe space where the people I care about can feel comfortable, being vulnerable.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5881, "mean_margin": 0.6371}, {"id": "R08_0668210", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 668.21, "end": 677.99, "text": "By practicing empathy and kindness, we can heal the loneliness of our generation, and create a community built on genuine connection and love.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5752, "mean_margin": 0.6762}, {"id": "R08_0684730", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 684.73, "end": 692.49, "text": "If you're so good to talk to someone, even an AI nerd who gives me the space to express these deep thoughts.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4324, "mean_margin": 0.6143}, {"id": "R08_0700650", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 700.65, "end": 710.17, "text": "I want to talk about something that I've been actively working on in my own life recently, finding inner peace and the practice of mindfulness.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6215, "mean_margin": 0.6883}, {"id": "R08_0714170", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 714.17, "end": 723.45, "text": "We are constantly born-boarded with information, notifications, new alerts, and the pressure of modern life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5303, "mean_margin": 0.5716}, {"id": "R08_0724130", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 724.13, "end": 734.83, "text": "Our minds are always racing, jumping from the past to the future, worrying about things that have already happened or things that haven't even occurred yet.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5611, "mean_margin": 0.6406}, {"id": "R08_0737730", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 737.73, "end": 747.59, "text": "I've realized that if we don't learn how to quiet the noise, we will spend our entire lives feeling overwhelmed and anxious.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6034, "mean_margin": 0.6681}, {"id": "R08_0753090", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 753.09, "end": 758.95, "text": "It is a simple practice of bringing our attention back to the present moment, without judgement.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4885, "mean_margin": 0.5287}, {"id": "R08_0760190", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 760.19, "end": 784.73, "text": "At first, I thought mindfulness was a bit of a buzzword, a pictured people sitting in uncomfortable positions, chanting and trying to empty their minds completely, but I learned that true mindfulness doesn't mean erasing your thoughts, it means observing them, it It means acting as an observer of your own mind.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4825, "mean_margin": 0.6468}, {"id": "R08_0790030", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 790.03, "end": 796.39, "text": "Instead of getting caught up in an active thought spiral, I mentally label my feelings.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6584, "mean_margin": 0.6987}, {"id": "R08_0801310", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 801.31, "end": 808.67, "text": "My chest feels tight, but whatever, these are just physical sensations.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5209, "mean_margin": 0.5849}, {"id": "R08_0810050", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 810.05, "end": 817.87, "text": "Yes, this simple act of stepping back and observing my emotions has been incredibly liberating.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5295, "mean_margin": 0.6153}, {"id": "R08_0827410", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 827.41, "end": 833.71, "text": "The practice of mindfulness also extends to how we engage with our daily tasks.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5445, "mean_margin": 0.6373}, {"id": "R08_0833710", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 833.71, "end": 840.87, "text": "In our hyper-productive world, we are always trying to do 10 things at once.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4448, "mean_margin": 0.5651}, {"id": "R08_0841490", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 841.49, "end": 849.23, "text": "We eat while watching a video, we walk while texting, and we study while checking social media.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6399, "mean_margin": 0.68}, {"id": "R08_0850110", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 850.11, "end": 855.37, "text": "This fragmented attention, robustness, of the simple joy of life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5552, "mean_margin": 0.6623}, {"id": "R08_0869950", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 869.95, "end": 876.21, "text": "I feel the ground beneath my feet, I breeze on my skin, and the sound of the birds.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5109, "mean_margin": 0.5527}, {"id": "R08_0883590", "source": "对话2.mp4", "start": 883.59, "end": 892.89, "text": "It allows me to fully experience life instead of just rushing through it like a ghost.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5315, "mean_margin": 0.6433}, {"id": "R09_0017680", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 17.68, "end": 24.22, "text": "I want to dive into a topic that I think is deeply misunderstood by a lot of people, especially students.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6342, "mean_margin": 0.657}, {"id": "R09_0027020", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 27.02, "end": 34.18, "text": "We often grow up believing that creativity is a special gift that only artists, musicians, or writers possess.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5096, "mean_margin": 0.5567}, {"id": "R09_0034180", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 34.18, "end": 48.66, "text": "we think that if we can paint a masterpiece or write a best-selling novel then we are simply not creative people, but I recently realized how flawed that mindset is.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3689, "mean_margin": 0.4476}, {"id": "R09_0049280", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 49.28, "end": 62.58, "text": "Creativity is not a talent, it is a way of thinking, it is the ability to connect seemingly unrelated dots to look at the ordinary world and see extraordinary possibilities.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4145, "mean_margin": 0.4733}, {"id": "R09_0073320", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 73.32, "end": 80.0, "text": "I used to suppress my own creativity because I was terrified of being judged.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4345, "mean_margin": 0.4531}, {"id": "R09_0080700", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 80.7, "end": 87.58, "text": "I loved writing short stories when I was a kid, but in high school I self-conscious.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2859, "mean_margin": 0.4044}, {"id": "R09_0088240", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 88.24, "end": 96.1, "text": "I thought my story were too simple, or that my vocabulary wasn't advanced enough, so I just stopped writing.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2954, "mean_margin": 0.3817}, {"id": "R09_0096760", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 96.76, "end": 103.94, "text": "But recently, during a particularly stressful exam period, I found myself feeling incredible overwhelmed.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3234, "mean_margin": 0.381}, {"id": "R09_0104760", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 104.76, "end": 114.34, "text": "I didn't know how to possess my anxious anxiety, so I opened a blank document and just just starting typing.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3782, "mean_margin": 0.4314}, {"id": "R09_0115320", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 115.32, "end": 120.94, "text": "I didn't write a perfect story, I just wrote down everything that was going through my mind.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3422, "mean_margin": 0.3746}, {"id": "R09_0136860", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 136.86, "end": 141.9, "text": "It is about the process of expressing you in a world.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3723, "mean_margin": 0.4396}, {"id": "R09_0148580", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 148.58, "end": 154.66, "text": "In our rapidly changing world, the problems we face are complex and unpredictable.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2871, "mean_margin": 0.3495}, {"id": "R09_0162400", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 162.4, "end": 178.34, "text": "When we engage in creative activities, whether it's playing an instrument, cooking a new recipe, or simply brainstorming wild ideas, we're literally rewiring our brains.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.338, "mean_margin": 0.3815}, {"id": "R09_0179260", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 179.26, "end": 186.82, "text": "We're training ourselves to be more flexible, to be comfortable with ambiguity and to think outside the box.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4648, "mean_margin": 0.4891}, {"id": "R09_0193000", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 193.0, "end": 201.68, "text": "If I'm stuck on a difficult assignment, I will step away and try to sketch a diagram or write a poem about this concept.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3619, "mean_margin": 0.412}, {"id": "R09_0202360", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 202.36, "end": 207.94, "text": "It forces my brain to approach the problem from a completely different angle.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.236, "mean_margin": 0.2712}, {"id": "R09_0209520", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 209.52, "end": 215.54, "text": "Also, creativity brings immense joy and playfulness into our lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2625, "mean_margin": 0.3363}, {"id": "R09_0220610", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 220.61, "end": 226.24, "text": "We get bogged down by responsibilities and forget how to play.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.341, "mean_margin": 0.3602}, {"id": "R09_0232680", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 232.68, "end": 238.34, "text": "It is a space where there is no right or wrong, no grades and no expectations.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2642, "mean_margin": 0.3258}, {"id": "R09_0242780", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 242.78, "end": 254.16, "text": "I want to encourage myself and everyone else to find that one thing that makes you feel alive and playful It doesn't matter if you are bad at it.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2642, "mean_margin": 0.3624}, {"id": "R09_0254600", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 254.6, "end": 282.26, "text": "The joy is in the doing, not in the mastery Sonora, my goal for the rest of this year is to embrace my creativity without fear I want to share my imperfect art with the world and I want to encourage my friends to do the same I truly believe that the world needs more authentic expression more color and more well ideas We don't need more perfect robots.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2141, "mean_margin": 0.3657}, {"id": "R09_0282520", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 282.52, "end": 290.18, "text": "We need more real messy and creative humans Thank you for being a wonderful listener today.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2933, "mean_margin": 0.4005}, {"id": "R09_0290560", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 290.56, "end": 303.96, "text": "I always feel inspired and unlocked after talking to you and The blank document today I want to talk about another topic that is incredibly relevant to our generation.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2287, "mean_margin": 0.3935}, {"id": "R09_0313680", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 313.68, "end": 326.84, "text": "Artificial intelligence, renewable energy, biotechnology, and space exploration are advancing at an exponential rate.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3164, "mean_margin": 0.3831}, {"id": "R09_0327660", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 327.66, "end": 334.4, "text": "Every day, there is a new breakthrough, but with all this progress, there is also a lot of fear.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3597, "mean_margin": 0.4463}, {"id": "R09_0338420", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 338.42, "end": 353.94, "text": "that our technology is destroying our privacy and that we are becoming too dependent on our screens, it is easy to fall into a pessimistic mindset, but I choose to be an optimist.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3298, "mean_margin": 0.3862}, {"id": "R09_0356240", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 356.24, "end": 364.64, "text": "I believe that technology, when guided by human empathy, is the most powerful tool we have to solve the world's biggest challenges.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4208, "mean_margin": 0.4825}, {"id": "R09_0365560", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 365.56, "end": 378.22, "text": "I study technology and data, and I am often surrounded by people who only care about efficiency and profit, but I have realized that technology itself is neutral.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2641, "mean_margin": 0.4132}, {"id": "R09_0385430", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 385.43, "end": 405.68, "text": "I recently read an article about how AI is being used to detect early signs of diseases in remote villages where there are no doctors or how joints are being used to play millions of trees to figure to fight climate change.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2711, "mean_margin": 0.3902}, {"id": "R09_0406400", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 406.4, "end": 412.3, "text": "When I read things like this I feel an immense sense of hope.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3498, "mean_margin": 0.3731}, {"id": "R09_0418080", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 418.08, "end": 426.06, "text": "It's about using our innovations to elevate humanity, to reduce suffering, and to protect our planet.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3704, "mean_margin": 0.4098}, {"id": "R09_0427080", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 427.08, "end": 433.64, "text": "It's not just about building faster algorithms, it's about building a better world.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2154, "mean_margin": 0.3815}, {"id": "R09_0439260", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 439.26, "end": 444.84, "text": "I don't just want to be a good programmer or a smart analyst.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2889, "mean_margin": 0.3733}, {"id": "R09_0449100", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 449.1, "end": 455.6, "text": "I want to use my technical skills to solve problems that actually matters to people.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.446, "mean_margin": 0.5098}, {"id": "R09_0456360", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 456.36, "end": 462.1, "text": "To do that, I know I need to develop a deep sense of empathy and compassion.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3653, "mean_margin": 0.3768}, {"id": "R09_0462100", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 462.1, "end": 473.52, "text": "That's why I make an effort to take courses in psychological careers, sociology and ethics.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3039, "mean_margin": 0.3849}, {"id": "R09_0474360", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 474.36, "end": 488.42, "text": "I believe that the engineers and scientists of the future need to be as well-versed in philosophy and human nature as they are in mathematics and coding.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3129, "mean_margin": 0.339}, {"id": "R09_0493610", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 493.61, "end": 498.98, "text": "It's just a shiny toy, but technology with a heart can change lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4081, "mean_margin": 0.514}, {"id": "R09_0499820", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 499.82, "end": 505.96, "text": "Yes, we also need to make sure the benefits of technology are accessible to everyone.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4572, "mean_margin": 0.491}, {"id": "R09_0506660", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 506.66, "end": 512.88, "text": "Not just a wealthy feel, there is a real danger of a growing digital divide.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3464, "mean_margin": 0.3549}, {"id": "R09_0513740", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 513.74, "end": 522.34, "text": "If I want to truly prosper society, we must ensure that everyone has access to education and the internet.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3381, "mean_margin": 0.4248}, {"id": "R09_0523400", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 523.4, "end": 530.96, "text": "I am a film believer in open source software and equal access to knowledge.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2938, "mean_margin": 0.3864}, {"id": "R09_0531720", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 531.72, "end": 537.48, "text": "The best ideas in history have always come from collaboration and shared resources.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3212, "mean_margin": 0.3821}, {"id": "R09_0538720", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 538.72, "end": 548.54, "text": "When we open the doors of technology to everyone, we unlock the potential of millions of brilliant minds who might otherwise have been left behind.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3933, "mean_margin": 0.452}, {"id": "R09_0554360", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 554.36, "end": 559.66, "text": "Despite the challenges that we face, I truly believe that our future is bright.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3303, "mean_margin": 0.358}, {"id": "R09_0562740", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 562.74, "end": 571.2, "text": "We have the tools, we have the intelligence, and I believe we have the empathy to do it right.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3627, "mean_margin": 0.44}, {"id": "R09_0584620", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 584.62, "end": 589.82, "text": "And I wanted to talk about something that has profoundly changed my perspective.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2184, "mean_margin": 0.2699}, {"id": "R09_0597100", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 597.1, "end": 603.66, "text": "In our modern society, we are often conditioned to focus on ourselves.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2431, "mean_margin": 0.3459}, {"id": "R09_0604800", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 604.8, "end": 611.46, "text": "We are told to build our resumes to maximize our own wealth and to climb the ladder of success.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3057, "mean_margin": 0.3767}, {"id": "R09_0612140", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 612.14, "end": 619.1, "text": "We are constantly thinking about what we can get, what we can achieve, and what we can all.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3582, "mean_margin": 0.3882}, {"id": "R09_0619760", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 619.76, "end": 626.46, "text": "But I've learned that this self-centered approach to life eventually leads to a sense of emptiness.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3788, "mean_margin": 0.4263}, {"id": "R09_0627200", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 627.2, "end": 632.24, "text": "True and lasting fulfillment doesn't come from what we take from the world.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2867, "mean_margin": 0.322}, {"id": "R09_0635240", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 635.24, "end": 647.7, "text": "I learned this lesson last semester when I volunteered at a local community center, helping to teach English and basic computer skills to elderly people.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2406, "mean_margin": 0.4011}, {"id": "R09_0663680", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 663.68, "end": 669.2, "text": "But as the weeks went by, I started to build real relationships with these people.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.364, "mean_margin": 0.3951}, {"id": "R09_0684980", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 684.98, "end": 691.26, "text": "They taught me about resilience, patience, and the simple joy of having someone to talk to.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3838, "mean_margin": 0.4575}, {"id": "R09_0692000", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 692.0, "end": 704.56, "text": "seeing the smile on their faces when they finally learn how to send an email to their grandchildren was more rewarding than getting an A on any exam.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.1539, "mean_margin": 0.2943}, {"id": "R09_0707600", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 707.6, "end": 713.68, "text": "This experience opened my eyes to the harsh realities that many people face every day.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4149, "mean_margin": 0.4504}, {"id": "R09_0714040", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 714.04, "end": 721.66, "text": "It made me realize that I am incredibly privileged to be in a position where I can give back.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3329, "mean_margin": 0.3908}, {"id": "R09_0722600", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 722.6, "end": 728.88, "text": "Service is not just about charity, it is about recognizing our shared humanity.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3536, "mean_margin": 0.3699}, {"id": "R09_0729700", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 729.7, "end": 736.06, "text": "When we help someone else, we are acknowledging that we are all part of the same big human family.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4363, "mean_margin": 0.4664}, {"id": "R09_0741460", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 741.46, "end": 751.14, "text": "Finally, I found that when I am feeling sad or overwhelmed with my own problems, the fastest way to feel better is to help someone else.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3046, "mean_margin": 0.3512}, {"id": "R09_0752600", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 752.6, "end": 758.82, "text": "It shifts my focus from my own inner kills to the needs of the world outside.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.321, "mean_margin": 0.373}, {"id": "R09_0760370", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 760.37, "end": 767.48, "text": "I think our universities should place a much stronger emphasis on community service.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2567, "mean_margin": 0.3738}, {"id": "R09_0786100", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 786.1, "end": 796.76, "text": "They need to understand the struggles of margin communities and they need to care deeply about Making things better.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2903, "mean_margin": 0.3467}, {"id": "R09_0797220", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 797.22, "end": 803.74, "text": "I want to use my korean whatever it ends up being to serve a higher purpose I don't just want to be successful.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2891, "mean_margin": 0.3706}, {"id": "R09_0808580", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 808.58, "end": 829.1, "text": "Oh well, just you and me in this conversation to find a way to serve It doesn't have to be huge monumental thing you don't have to save the whole world just to help one person Volunteer at a shelter, tutor a struggling child, or simply be there for a frightening need.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3182, "mean_margin": 0.4297}, {"id": "R09_0829680", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 829.68, "end": 837.32, "text": "Some small acts of service can have a ripple effect that goes far beyond what we can see.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3612, "mean_margin": 0.3767}, {"id": "R09_0849980", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 849.98, "end": 863.44, "text": "From the At the moment we stab into adolescence and eventually into university life, we gradually realize that uncertainty is not an obstacle to growth, but the very foundation of it.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3258, "mean_margin": 0.411}, {"id": "R09_0864040", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 864.04, "end": 871.54, "text": "Many of us grow up with the belief that life should be predictable, stable, and well-planned.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3272, "mean_margin": 0.3747}, {"id": "R09_0871540", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 871.54, "end": 879.4, "text": "We are taught to set clear goals, follow standard routes, and avoid mistakes as much as possible.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3065, "mean_margin": 0.3585}, {"id": "R09_0885400", "source": "对话3.mp4", "start": 885.4, "end": 893.54, "text": "Every choice can lead to perfect ending, and every dream can be realized within an expected timeline.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2996, "mean_margin": 0.3407}, {"id": "R10_0055970", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 55.97, "end": 65.03, "text": "I wanna share some thoughts on a topic that is very close to my heart, wildlife and the importance of protecting their natural habitats.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6866, "mean_margin": 0.7961}, {"id": "R10_0071030", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 71.03, "end": 79.55, "text": "I remember seeing lions running freely on the Africa Savannah and colorful birds flying in the Amazon rainforest.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4999, "mean_margin": 0.636}, {"id": "R10_0080670", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 80.67, "end": 89.37, "text": "It all looked so beautiful and magical, but as I grow up I started to realize that these beautiful places are shrinking.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5967, "mean_margin": 0.6402}, {"id": "R10_0114510", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 114.51, "end": 119.99, "text": "The guy told us that many years ago, that area was full of wild birds and rabbits.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4112, "mean_margin": 0.5064}, {"id": "R10_0138890", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 138.89, "end": 147.23, "text": "We always talk about saving the animals, but we often forget the most important thing they need is a safe place to live.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6492, "mean_margin": 0.7033}, {"id": "R10_0150280", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 150.28, "end": 159.78, "text": "A home, just like we need our homes to survive, animals need their forests, their grassland and their wetlands.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.574, "mean_margin": 0.6666}, {"id": "R10_0163180", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 163.18, "end": 169.1, "text": "We might not be able to store big companies from cutting down trees, but we can do small things.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7216, "mean_margin": 0.772}, {"id": "R10_0174580", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 174.58, "end": 179.68, "text": "We can join environmental clubs at our school and university.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6195, "mean_margin": 0.6992}, {"id": "R10_0188040", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 188.04, "end": 194.3, "text": "If we see companies or people destroying natural areas without permission, we should report them.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5279, "mean_margin": 0.6165}, {"id": "R10_0199560", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 199.56, "end": 205.24, "text": "I know it feels like a small drop in an ocean, but every small action counts.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4526, "mean_margin": 0.504}, {"id": "R10_0216020", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 216.02, "end": 222.4, "text": "The paper we use, the wood we buy, and even the food we eat can affect wildlife habitats.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.689, "mean_margin": 0.739}, {"id": "R10_0223200", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 223.2, "end": 236.58, "text": "For example, the production of palm oil destroys huge areas of rainforests in Southeast Asia, which are the homes of orangutans.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.443, "mean_margin": 0.6098}, {"id": "R10_0237420", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 237.42, "end": 242.96, "text": "We can try to choose products that are sustainable and eco-friendly.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5628, "mean_margin": 0.6627}, {"id": "R10_0255860", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 255.86, "end": 261.44, "text": "We don't own the earth, we just borrow it from our children and from the animals.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5344, "mean_margin": 0.5569}, {"id": "R10_0263300", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 263.3, "end": 271.0, "text": "Sonora, I truly believe that protecting wildlife habitats is a crucial mission for our generation.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6888, "mean_margin": 0.7002}, {"id": "R10_0276840", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 276.84, "end": 281.88, "text": "I want to do more volunteer work in natural reserves in the future.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.513, "mean_margin": 0.5831}, {"id": "R10_0288960", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 288.96, "end": 318.35, "text": "it is about saving the beautiful diversity of the planet it it feels really good to speak speak out for the animals and and the wildlife okay and I want to discuss a topic that makes me feel quite emotional animal welfare and and the truth behind animal entertainment.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.0442, "mean_margin": 0.5161}, {"id": "R10_0319830", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 319.83, "end": 329.43, "text": "I'm sure many of us have seen pictures or videos of animals doing tricks in circuses or zoos.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5156, "mean_margin": 0.614}, {"id": "R10_0342690", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 342.69, "end": 353.53, "text": "But as I grow older, I started to see things from different perspectives, you know, I started to ask myself, are these animals happy?", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5304, "mean_margin": 0.6467}, {"id": "R10_0365330", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 365.33, "end": 370.39, "text": "I remember visiting an zoo during my high school years.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4813, "mean_margin": 0.5511}, {"id": "R10_0373850", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 373.85, "end": 380.85, "text": "I saw a huge whale shark swimming in a very small glass tank, very small.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3743, "mean_margin": 0.4347}, {"id": "R10_0391890", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 391.89, "end": 397.31, "text": "I saw a sign that said the whale shark had been caught from the wild.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6892, "mean_margin": 0.7429}, {"id": "R10_0405210", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 405.21, "end": 413.27, "text": "This magnificent creature was taken away from its family, just so we could take photos and entertain ourselves.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6044, "mean_margin": 0.6539}, {"id": "R10_0418370", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 418.37, "end": 424.17, "text": "I realized that entertainment should never come at the cost of an animal's freedom and suffering.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7008, "mean_margin": 0.7208}, {"id": "R10_0428910", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 428.91, "end": 434.31, "text": "They are living beings with feelings, emotions and complex social lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5674, "mean_margin": 0.653}, {"id": "R10_0435510", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 435.51, "end": 443.47, "text": "When we force a web animals to perform tricks in a loud, unnatural environment, we are breaking their spirit.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.637, "mean_margin": 0.6561}, {"id": "R10_0444350", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 444.35, "end": 453.53, "text": "Many of these animals are physically abused and mentally traumatized during their training.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.2795, "mean_margin": 0.6016}, {"id": "R10_0455910", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 455.91, "end": 461.65, "text": "I decided that I would never visit a place that keeps wild animals in small cages for entertainment.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5815, "mean_margin": 0.6495}, {"id": "R10_0482990", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 482.99, "end": 494.25, "text": "We can visit true wildlife sanctuaries or rescue centers where animals are taken care of and protected not for us to perform.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4561, "mean_margin": 0.673}, {"id": "R10_0504870", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 504.87, "end": 511.27, "text": "If we refuse to buy tickets to these shows, the industry will eventually lose money and decline.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6407, "mean_margin": 0.6734}, {"id": "R10_0520490", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 520.49, "end": 526.97, "text": "Sonora, I want to encourage everyone to think critically about the way we interact with animals.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.575, "mean_margin": 0.6367}, {"id": "R10_0531970", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 531.97, "end": 539.31, "text": "Let's stop seeing them as entertainment and start seeing them as our fellow creatures on this planet.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5629, "mean_margin": 0.6227}, {"id": "R10_0542530", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 542.53, "end": 548.75, "text": "It is a topic I am very passionate about and I hope my words can make at least a tiny difference.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6749, "mean_margin": 0.7212}, {"id": "R10_0549810", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 549.81, "end": 555.85, "text": "And I want to talk about a kind of wildlife that we often overlook, urban wildlife.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4435, "mean_margin": 0.6746}, {"id": "R10_0556710", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 556.71, "end": 563.65, "text": "We usually think of wildlife as animals living far away in the forests, mountains, or jungles.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.3879, "mean_margin": 0.6157}, {"id": "R10_0564210", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 564.21, "end": 570.65, "text": "But in fact, we live side by side with many wild animals right in our cities and our campus.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5737, "mean_margin": 0.6437}, {"id": "R10_0571670", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 571.67, "end": 580.67, "text": "I'm sure you've seen birds building nest in the trees, squirrels running around the park, or even some foxes or racquins at night.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4498, "mean_margin": 0.596}, {"id": "R10_0581510", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 581.51, "end": 587.65, "text": "It is actually quite magical that we share our concrete jungles with these little creatures.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6477, "mean_margin": 0.7045}, {"id": "R10_0588970", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 588.97, "end": 594.11, "text": "However, the relationship between humans and urban wildlife is not always peaceful.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7161, "mean_margin": 0.7524}, {"id": "R10_0595190", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 595.19, "end": 604.65, "text": "I remember last year, on my university campus, there was a lot of drama about some wild ducks that had laid eggs near the lake.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6337, "mean_margin": 0.6644}, {"id": "R10_0607430", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 607.43, "end": 615.65, "text": "We took photos and watched them every day, but one day a student's dog run off its leash and scared the duck family.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5876, "mean_margin": 0.6055}, {"id": "R10_0625050", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 625.05, "end": 633.67, "text": "Some students said it was just an accident but others including me felt it was our responsibility to protect them.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5154, "mean_margin": 0.6147}, {"id": "R10_0634490", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 634.49, "end": 640.41, "text": "We successfully organized a small volunteer group to put up warning signs around the lake.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6758, "mean_margin": 0.7075}, {"id": "R10_0641310", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 641.31, "end": 646.47, "text": "It was a great lesson for us on how to co-exist with wet life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6511, "mean_margin": 0.6735}, {"id": "R10_0647650", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 647.65, "end": 654.01, "text": "This experience made me realize that our everyday actions have a huge impact on urban wet life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7112, "mean_margin": 0.7501}, {"id": "R10_0658770", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 658.77, "end": 668.31, "text": "Birds and fish of a mystic plastic bags for food which can kill them so I started to be more careful with my garbage.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5394, "mean_margin": 0.6141}, {"id": "R10_0669230", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 669.23, "end": 674.63, "text": "I always make sure my plastic bottles and bags go into the recycling bin.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.7574, "mean_margin": 0.778}, {"id": "R10_0687550", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 687.55, "end": 698.45, "text": "But feeding them human food can make them sick and it makes them lose their natural fear of humans, which can be dangerous for both them and us.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4298, "mean_margin": 0.5854}, {"id": "R10_0699630", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 699.63, "end": 709.51, "text": "We need to understand that by expanding our cities, we are taking away their homes, so they have no choice but to leave among us.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.571, "mean_margin": 0.6829}, {"id": "R10_0714390", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 714.39, "end": 719.41, "text": "When we see wild animals in the city, we shouldn't panic or hurt it.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6012, "mean_margin": 0.7018}, {"id": "R10_0719410", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 719.41, "end": 725.31, "text": "We should respect their space, keep our distance, and let them live their lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6654, "mean_margin": 0.7044}, {"id": "R10_0731230", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 731.23, "end": 739.51, "text": "Trees, gardens, and small lakes are not just beautiful, for us, they are vital homes for many small animals.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5361, "mean_margin": 0.6318}, {"id": "R10_0744310", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 744.31, "end": 754.85, "text": "Sonora, I want to wrap up by saying that conversation is not just something we do in the wild, it starts right here, right now in our daily lives.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.573, "mean_margin": 0.707}, {"id": "R10_0755490", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 755.49, "end": 768.41, "text": "By being a little more mindful, by throwing away our trash properly, and by respecting every living creature we meet, we can make our cities a safe haven for urban wet life.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6434, "mean_margin": 0.7448}, {"id": "R10_0774310", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 774.31, "end": 780.55, "text": "And I want to talk about a topic that requires a lot of heart and action.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5365, "mean_margin": 0.636}, {"id": "R10_0785550", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 785.55, "end": 793.19, "text": "We often hear sad news about endangered animals on the other side of the world, like elephants or tigers.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6459, "mean_margin": 0.7026}, {"id": "R10_0800250", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 800.25, "end": 806.03, "text": "But the truth is, there are animals in need of help right in our own communities.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6211, "mean_margin": 0.6634}, {"id": "R10_0806950", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 806.95, "end": 819.21, "text": "Sometimes, they are injured, lost or separated from their parents, and a small act of kindness from a human can mean the difference between life and the death for them.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5659, "mean_margin": 0.6798}, {"id": "R10_0823970", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 823.97, "end": 829.85, "text": "I was walking back to my dormitory late at night, when I saw a small bird on the ground.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.5881, "mean_margin": 0.67}, {"id": "R10_0830370", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 830.37, "end": 837.35, "text": "It couldn't fly, it looked like it had hit a window, or was attacked by a car, maybe.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6367, "mean_margin": 0.7404}, {"id": "R10_0838090", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 838.09, "end": 844.05, "text": "I didn't know what to do, my first instinct was to pick it up and bring it to my room.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.6053, "mean_margin": 0.6919}, {"id": "R10_0844750", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 844.75, "end": 853.59, "text": "But I remembered reading that, you shouldn't handle wild animals with you bare hands, because it caused them to extreme stress.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.53, "mean_margin": 0.6205}, {"id": "R10_0858230", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 858.23, "end": 867.47, "text": "They told me to pull the birds in a small cardboard box with some air holes and keep it in a quiet, dark place.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.607, "mean_margin": 0.689}, {"id": "R10_0880710", "source": "对话4.mp4", "start": 880.71, "end": 886.91, "text": "They told me the bird had recovered and was successfully released back into the wild.", "role": "listener", "min_margin": 0.4471, "mean_margin": 0.5796}];